update public.tips set body_md = 'The little word matches the thing, not you: **un** té, **un** helado, but **una** torta, **una** pizza. Learn each new word with its *un* or *una* and you''ll never have to guess. One twist: *agua* takes **un** — *un agua*. It is still an *una* word, though: *otra agua*.' where id = 'fbdb815c-fea1-52ae-84c1-af98b2814484' and body_md = 'The little word matches the thing, not you: **un** té, **un** helado, but **una** torta, **una** pizza. Learn each new word with its *un* or *una* and you''ll never have to guess. One twist: *agua* takes **un** — *un agua*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To say who you are, use **soy**: *Soy Sofi.* One word carries "I am". The word for "I" (**yo**) is usually left out; add it only to stress or contrast: *Yo soy Martín.*' where id = '03c07d66-92a9-54f3-842f-c123a1a62c76' and body_md = 'To say who you are, use **soy**: *Soy Sofi.* One word carries "I am" . The word for "I" (**yo**) is usually left out; add it only to stress or contrast: *Yo soy Martín.*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When someone says *gracias*, answer **de nada**. *Of course* is **claro**. And when everything is fine or agreed, porteños say **¡joya!** — *¿Todo bien? — ¡Joya!*' where id = '73cc59dc-ddb9-5779-b542-a35b9fd331ff' and body_md = 'When someone says *gracias*, answer **de nada**. *Of course* is **claro**. And when something''s sorted, porteños say **¡joya!** — *¿Todo bien? — ¡Joya!*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Stuck on a word: **¿cómo se dice…?** — *how do you say…?* — and **¿qué significa?** — *what does it mean?* Too fast: **más despacio, por favor**. And the line that makes people slow down and help: **hablo un poco** — *I speak a little*. Argentines call the language **castellano**.' where id = '1f4b9651-418e-5f8c-a3bf-03626d36a760' and body_md = 'Stuck on a word: **¿cómo se dice…?** — *how do you say…?* — and **¿qué significa?** — *what does it mean?* Too fast: **más despacio, por favor**. And the line that buys you patience: **hablo un poco** — *I speak a little*. Argentines call the language **castellano**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Two forms of *ser* so far: **soy** for yourself, **sos** for the person in front of you. *Soy Lucía, ¿y vos?* — *¿Sos turista?* The words *yo* and *vos* are optional; the verb already says who.' where id = '6620174b-7e7e-5f88-a3b7-17aa03b97032' and body_md = 'Two forms of *ser* so far: **soy** for yourself, **sos** for the person in front of you. *Soy Lucía, ¿y vos?* — *¿Sos turista?* The pronoun is optional; the verb already says who.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Three people, three forms of *ser*:

| yo | **soy** |
| vos | **sos** |
| él, ella | **es** |

The verb already tells you who, so *él* or *ella* is usually dropped: *Es de Rosario* — he''s (or she''s) from Rosario.' where id = '03fc2a95-8aca-5aee-8293-e0768e0f0df9' and body_md = 'Three people, three forms of *ser*:

| yo | **soy** |
| vos | **sos** |
| él, ella | **es** |

The verb already tells you who, so the pronoun is usually dropped: *Es de Rosario* — he''s (or she''s) from Rosario.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Quién** asks *who*: *¿Quién es él?* The answer drops *él* or *ella*: *Es Martín, un vecino.* Whose? Use **de**: *una amiga de Juan* — *a friend of Juan''s*. A **pibe** is a young guy and a **piba** a young woman — very porteño.' where id = 'fde51102-e5bd-5f88-9d8d-8656cc371174' and body_md = '**Quién** asks *who*: *¿Quién es él?* The answer drops the pronoun: *Es Martín, un vecino.* Whose? Use **de**: *una amiga de Juan* — *a friend of Juan''s*. A **pibe** is a young guy and a **piba** a young woman — very porteño.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**No entendí** — *I didn''t understand* — is what you say when you missed something just said: *Perdón, no entendí. ¿Me repetís?* It is the past of *no entiendo*. Add *más despacio, por favor* and people slow down.', title_en = 'No entendí' where id = '95b906a1-cab6-5656-9bd4-7597c0a6238b' and body_md = 'Stuck on a word: **¿cómo se dice…?** — *how do you say…?* — and **¿qué significa?** — *what does it mean?* Too fast: **¿me repetís?** or **más despacio, por favor**. **No entendí** is *I didn''t get that*. And the line that buys you patience: **hablo un poco de castellano** — Argentines call the language *castellano*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Words for people follow the person: *mi tío, mi tía*; *brasileño, brasileña*. A word in *-e* stays put: *canadiense*. A nationality ending in a consonant adds *-a*, and any accent mark goes: *francés → francesa*, *español → española*.' where id = 'd244b49a-e1eb-5cb3-9ae8-b0efee8aa45d' and body_md = 'Words for people follow the person: *mi tío, mi tía*; *brasileño, brasileña*. A word in *-e* stays put: *canadiense*. One ending in a consonant adds *-a*: *francés → francesa*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'An **alfajor** is two soft cookies stuck together with *dulce de leche*, often dipped in chocolate. Every kiosco (the corner shop) sells them, and every porteño has a favorite.' where id = 'c99796c8-7e24-5a5d-ab39-3c8321dd111c' and body_md = 'An **alfajor** is two soft biscuits stuck together with *dulce de leche*, often dipped in chocolate. Every kiosco sells them, and every porteño has a favorite.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A **kiosco** is the corner shop that sells drinks, sweets and cigarettes and tops up your SUBE (the bus and subway card), often through a window onto the street. Many are open all night.' where id = '81f0edea-517c-5fc8-a10c-abf8f72ba4fa' and body_md = 'A **kiosco** is the corner shop that sells drinks, sweets and bus cards, often through a window onto the street. Many never close.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| something new | something you already know |
| **Hay** un kiosco. | **El** kiosco **está** en la esquina. |
| **Hay** una parada acá. | **La** parada **está** lejos. |

**Hay** goes with *un, una*, a number or nothing at all, and never changes: *hay dos kioscos*, *¿hay agua?* **Está** goes with *el, la*.', title_en = 'Hay or está' where id = 'ec69da9b-919b-5227-808d-abb58a8beed8' and body_md = '| something new | something you already know |
| **Hay** un kiosco. | **El** kiosco **está** en la esquina. |
| **Hay** una parada acá. | **La** parada **está** lejos. |
**Hay** goes with *un, una*, a number or no little word at all, and never changes: *hay dos kioscos*, *¿hay agua?* **Está** goes with *el, la*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'No *la* before home: **estoy en casa**, *I''m at home*. With anything else you need *el* or *la*: *en la mochila*, *en el auto*.' where id = '4a5c7164-2735-57f0-a2e7-64e4f99cc52c' and body_md = 'No *la* before home: **estoy en casa**, *I''m at home*. With anything else the little word comes back: *en la mochila*, *en el auto*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Su** is *his*, *her* or *their* (and *your* for *ustedes*); with more than one it is **sus**: *su mamá*, *sus hijos*. *Our* matches the thing, not the people: **nuestro** papá, **nuestra** familia, **nuestros** abuelos, **nuestras** hermanas.', title_en = 'Su and nuestro' where id = '040623f8-7ca5-5206-8e5c-f178b0d6fbe4' and body_md = '**Su** is *his*, *her* or *their* — and *your* for *ustedes*. Like *mi* and *tu*, it takes an *-s* with more than one: *su mamá*, *sus hijos*. The rest of the sentence tells you whose.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Listo** is *ready* — *¿estás lista?* — and on its own it closes any deal: *Listo, dale.* **Apurado** is *in a hurry*, the normal state of anyone downtown.' where id = 'fc0b4b4e-f184-5ab8-adcb-2352ae9cdeae' and body_md = '**Listo** is *ready* — *¿estás lista?* — and on its own it closes any deal: *Listo, dale.* **Apurado** is *in a hurry*, the normal state of anyone in the centro.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Porteños say **a la noche** for *at night* or *tonight*: *A la noche estudio inglés.* *Hablamos a la noche* — we''ll talk tonight. **De noche** is at night in general: *laburo de noche* (I work nights). And **¿qué hacés?** — literally *what are you doing?* — is also the everyday *how''s it going?*: *Hola, ¿qué hacés?*' where id = '9b8de7a7-8ce6-5500-a8ab-a7d35c9c940e' and body_md = 'Porteños say **a la noche** for *at night* or *tonight*: *A la noche estudio inglés.* *Hablamos a la noche* — we''ll talk tonight. **De noche** is at night in general: *laburo de noche*. And **¿qué hacés?** — literally *what are you doing?* — is also the everyday *how''s it going?*: *Hola, ¿qué hacés?*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Take off *-ar* and add the ending for the person:

| yo | labur**o** |
| vos | labur**ás** |
| él, ella | labur**a** |
| nosotros | labur**amos** |
| ellos, ustedes | labur**an** |

It works for *hablar, tomar, estudiar, caminar* — every regular -ar verb. **Hacer** is not an -ar verb, so learn its three forms as they are: **hago**, *hacés, hace*.' where id = '3df4bd97-1130-5b76-9ad3-39e06c420e6b' and body_md = 'Take off *-ar* and add the ending for the person:

| yo | labur**o** |
| vos | labur**ás** |
| él, ella | labur**a** |
| nosotros | labur**amos** |
| ellos, ustedes | labur**an** |

It works for *hablar, tomar, estudiar, caminar* — every regular -ar verb. **Hacer** is irregular in *yo*: **hago**, *hacés, hace*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The verb matches the thing you like, not you: *Me **gusta** el mate*, but *Me **gustan** las facturas*. The little word in front says who likes it: **me**, **te**, **le**. With a name, add **a** and keep **le**: *A Lucía le gusta el mate.*', title_en = 'Gusta or gustan' where id = '1861263d-ed73-5540-a7c8-6bd95804c94e' and body_md = 'The verb matches the thing you like, not you:
| one thing | more than one |
| Me **gusta** el mate. | Me **gustan** las facturas. |
| ¿Te **gusta** la milanesa? | ¿Te **gustan** los mates? |
**Me** — to me, **te** — to you, **le** — to him or her. For emphasis, add *a mí*: *A mí me gusta amargo.* With a name you need **a** and **le**: *A Lucía le gusta el mate.* Short answers: *A mí sí. A mí no.* With a verb it''s always *gusta*: *me gusta tomar mate*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The little word in front says who likes it: **me**, **te**, **le**, **nos**, **les**. The verb is only ever *gusta* (one thing) or *gustan* (several): *le gust**a** el pollo*, *me gust**an** las medialunas*.', title_en = 'Who likes it' where id = 'a7aca477-d93f-5ae8-8217-3f52071a1d8f' and body_md = 'With *gustar* the person goes in front: **me** gusta, **te** gusta, **le** gusta, **nos** gusta, **les** gusta. Only *gusta* or *gustan* ever changes after it.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| asking | **¿Hay** una estación **por acá**? |
| yes | Sí, **hay** una en la avenida. |
| no | No, acá no **hay** tren. |
| where | La estación **está** a dos cuadras. |

**Por acá** is *around here*. **Hay** never changes: *hay un bar*, *hay dos plazas*, *hay gente*. ' where id = 'c41cf955-fb7f-5670-b1e2-cc4a2a59f30c' and body_md = '| asking | **¿Hay** una estación **por acá**? |
| yes | Sí, **hay** una en la avenida. |
| no | No, acá no **hay** tren. |
| where | La estación **está** a dos cuadras. |

**Hay** never changes: *hay un bar*, *hay dos plazas*, *hay gente*. ';
update public.tips set body_md = 'In Argentina the waiter is **el mozo** (or *la moza*). To call one over, *perdón* is the gentle way; *¡mozo!* is heard too. When you''re done, ask for **la cuenta**. ' where id = '5accb3e5-9f5d-571b-b159-856ad4feb161' and body_md = 'In Argentina the waiter is **el mozo** (or *la moza*). To call one over, *perdón* is the gentle way; *¡mozo!* is heard too. When you''re done, ask for **la cuenta**. A **cortado** is an espresso with a dash of milk.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Ordering for more than one: **queremos** dos cafés. The mozo asks the table **¿qué quieren?** And for someone else: *ella **quiere** un té*. The *ie* is everywhere except *querés* and *queremos*.' where id = 'bce85693-14c0-55df-9f48-e478356528a2' and body_md = 'Ordering for more than one: **queremos** dos cortados. The mozo asks the table **¿qué quieren?** And for someone else: *ella **quiere** un té*. The *ie* is everywhere except *querés* and *queremos*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The easy way to order is to ask the waiter to bring it: **¿Me traés un café?** — literally "do you bring me a coffee?". *Quiero un café* works too: **quiero**, **¿querés?** — no *ie* in the vos form. Or just name it: *Para mí, un té.* Add **por favor**.' where id = '6c6949b3-904f-59fe-8a19-085c5f916515' and body_md = 'The easy way to order is to ask the waiter to bring it: **¿Me traés un café?** — literally "do you bring me a coffee?". *Quiero un café* works too: **quiero**, **¿querés?** — no *ie* in the vos form. Add **por favor**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Tener que** + an infinitive (the *-ar, -er, -ir* form) is *to have to*: *tengo que laburar* — I have to work; *¿tenés que estudiar?* — do you have to study? A different **que** joins two ideas: *tengo una jefa que habla inglés* — a boss who speaks English.', title_en = 'Tener que, and que' where id = 'ae41a407-af9b-5cde-9ad6-f0b967fd6c3a' and body_md = '**Tener que** + an infinitive — the *-ar, -er, -ir* form — is *to have to*:

| Tengo que laburar. | I have to work. |
| ¿Tenés que estudiar? | Do you have to study? |

Jobs change for a woman: *profesor* → **profesora**, *médico* → **médica**, *jefe* → **jefa**. And no *un, una*: **Soy abogada.** **Que** also joins two ideas: *tengo una jefa que habla inglés* — a boss who speaks English.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Facu** is short for *facultad* — university. For jobs, Spanish drops the article: **Soy profesora**, not *soy una profesora*. Jobs change for a woman: *profesor* → **profesora**, *médico* → **médica**, *jefe* → **jefa**.' where id = '2375ef12-8a94-5b13-ba9c-dfbfe8356608' and body_md = '**Facu** is short for *facultad* — university. For jobs, Spanish drops the article: **Soy profesora**, not *soy una profesora*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| yo | **tengo que** laburar |
| vos | **tenés que** practicar |
| él, ella | **tiene que** ayudar |
| nosotros | **tenemos que** estudiar |
| ellos, ustedes | **tienen que** buscar a sus hijos |

Jobs: *enfermero* → **enfermera**, *vendedor* → **vendedora**; *periodista* and *policía* stay the same. ' where id = '4c58f6d8-63be-595e-abec-599eea09eb64' and body_md = '| yo | **tengo que** laburar |
| vos | **tenés que** practicar |
| él, ella | **tiene que** ayudar |
| nosotros | **tenemos que** estudiar |
| ellos, ustedes | **tienen que** buscar a sus hijos |

Jobs: *enfermero* → **enfermera**, *vendedor* → **vendedora**; *periodista* and *policía* stay the same. No *un, una*: **Es contadora.**';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | comer | vivir |
| yo | com**o** | viv**o** |
| vos | com**és** | viv**ís** |
| él, ella | com**e** | viv**e** |
| nosotros | com**emos** | viv**imos** |
| ellos, ustedes | com**en** | viv**en** |

-er and -ir are the same except for **vos** and **nosotros**, where each keeps its own vowel. The present also covers *I''m eating* and a near future: *te escribo a la noche* — I''ll write to you tonight.' where id = '56d4a95b-8525-5ac4-8df6-3c26ebc33762' and body_md = '| | comer | vivir |
| yo | com**o** | viv**o** |
| vos | com**és** | viv**ís** |
| él, ella | com**e** | viv**e** |
| nosotros | com**emos** | viv**imos** |
| ellos, ustedes | com**en** | viv**en** |

-er and -ir are the same except for **vos** and **nosotros**, where each keeps its own vowel.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Abrir** and **recibir** are regular: *abro, abrís, abre*; *recibo, recibís, recibe*. *¿El negocio abre a la noche?* **Recibir a** someone is to have them over: *recibo a mi suegra*.' where id = '5f609aca-4b7c-5585-9e3f-2d151bb4c25c' and body_md = '**Abrir** and **recibir** are regular: *abro, abrís, abre*; *recibo, recibís, recibe*. *¿El negocio abre a la noche?*';
update public.tips set body_md = '-er verbs keep **e** and -ir verbs take **i**, but only for *vos* and *nosotros*: *vend**és**, vend**emos*** but *abr**ís**, abr**imos***. Everywhere else they match: *vendo, abro*; *lee, comparte*; *leen, escriben*. *Recibir* and *correr* follow the same pattern.', title_en = '-er and -ir: different only in vos and nosotros' where id = 'ff18c38c-372c-591e-a3e1-3ae0c2d65dfc' and body_md = '| | leer | compartir | escribir |
| yo | le**o** | compart**o** | escrib**o** |
| vos | le**és** | compart**ís** | escrib**ís** |
| él, ella | le**e** | compart**e** | escrib**e** |
| nosotros | le**emos** | compart**imos** | escrib**imos** |
| ellos, ustedes | le**en** | compart**en** | escrib**en** |

-er keeps **e** and -ir takes **i**, but only for *vos* and *nosotros*: *vend**és**, vend**emos*** but *abr**ís**, abr**imos***. *Recibir* and *correr* follow the same pattern: *recibo, recibís, recibe*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Negocio** is any shop, not just a business: *el negocio de la esquina*. And porteños **comparten** everything, from an apartment to a mate. *Con mi hermano vendemos empanadas* means *my brother and I sell* — two people, not three.' where id = '9769b812-efcf-50e2-8dd0-7a43d62e3f1b' and body_md = '**Negocio** is any shop, not just a business: *el negocio de la esquina*. And porteños **comparten** everything, from an apartment to a mate.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The *ellos* and *ustedes* form of every verb you have ends in **-n**: *quieren, tienen, laburan, viven, escriben*. *¿Quieren café?* — do you guys want coffee? Hear the *-n* and you know it''s more than one.' where id = '63ff509a-3d7b-5687-a565-dd402adb7b88' and body_md = 'The *ellos* form of every verb you have ends in **-n**: *quieren, tienen, laburan, viven, escriben*. Hear the *-n* and you know it''s more than one.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The ground floor is **la planta baja**; above it comes *el **primer** piso* (*primero* loses its *-o* before a noun). Then **segundo, tercero, cuarto, quinto**. Higher up, people often just say the number: *piso doce*. On the **timbre**, *4° B* is read **cuarto B**. **Piso** is also the floor you walk on.', title_en = 'Planta baja y pisos' where id = 'd8622385-5e4a-5495-9a55-b9f96b8c8aeb' and body_md = 'The ground floor is **la planta baja**; the one above it is *el primer piso*. Ringing from the street, you press the **timbre** with the floor and the letter: *4° B*. Out loud, *4° B* is **cuarto B**: *vivo en el cuarto B*. The first five floors: **primero, segundo, tercero, cuarto, quinto** — and *primero* loses its *-o* before a noun: *el **primer** piso*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Most buildings have an **encargado** who lives in the building, keeps it clean and takes in your packages. He knows everything that happens on every **piso**.' where id = 'c538de60-17a3-5573-95d5-96e0be486781' and body_md = 'Most buildings have an **encargado** who lives in, keeps it clean and takes in your packages. He knows everything that happens on every **piso**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Argentines say **depto** for an apartment, **pieza** for a bedroom and **el living** for the living room. The fridge is **la heladera**. **Alquilo** on its own means *I rent my place*: *¿Dónde alquilás?*' where id = 'f9a1e455-91a4-5b1f-89f4-59d39156345f' and body_md = 'Argentines say **depto** for an apartment, **pieza** for a bedroom and **el living** for the living room. The fridge is **la heladera**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Days take **el** for one day and **los** for every week: *el miércoles laburo* (on Wednesday), *los lunes laburo* (on Mondays). They have no capital letter. Dates work the same way, with a plain number: *el veintiuno tengo examen*.', title_en = 'El lunes, los lunes' where id = 'afc27211-febc-5355-9843-5cd952ec9052' and body_md = 'Twenty-one to twenty-nine are one word: **veintiuno**, **veintidós**, **veintitrés**. From thirty on, **y** joins them: *treinta y uno*, *cuarenta y cinco*. A hundred is **cien**. For *on* a day, use **el**: *el miércoles laburo*, *el veintiuno tengo examen*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '*Es la una* (one o''clock), but *son las dos*, *son las siete*. Add **y media** for half past and **y cuarto** for quarter past. Other minutes go the same way: *las siete y veinte*. To ask: *¿Qué hora es?* or *¿Tenés hora?* *At* a time is **a las**: *¿A qué hora?* — *A las nueve y media.* After a clock time say **de la mañana / de la tarde / de la noche**: *a las dos de la tarde*. With no clock time: **a la mañana**, *a la tarde*, *a la noche*.' where id = '97b6abce-e595-58cb-a895-30319da57ada' and body_md = '*Es la una* (one o''clock), but *son las dos*, *son las siete*. Add **y media** for half past and **y cuarto** for quarter past. *At* a time is **a las**: *¿A qué hora?* — *A las nueve y media.* After a clock time say **de la mañana / de la tarde / de la noche**: *a las dos de la tarde*. With no clock time: **a la mañana**, *a la tarde*, *a la noche*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Opening hours are **desde** … **hasta**: *abre desde las nueve hasta las seis*. Shorter, and more common: *abre **de** nueve **a** seis*. At twelve it''s **el mediodía** — and plenty of small shops **cierran** for a while right after it. With **desde**, Spanish uses the present: *estoy acá desde las ocho* = I''ve been here since eight.' where id = '7782b8c8-3797-5039-896a-6aeac6b65951' and body_md = 'Opening hours are **desde** … **hasta**: *abre desde las nueve hasta las seis*. Shorter, and more common: *abre **de** nueve **a** seis*. At twelve it''s **el mediodía** — and plenty of small shops **cierran** for a while right after it.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'At the front desk one line does it: **tengo una reserva a nombre de** … and your name. They will ask for your **pasaporte**. Staying two nights? *Dos noches.*' where id = '52586356-7f20-5175-b293-6a0dd0d21654' and body_md = 'At the front desk one line does it: **tengo una reserva a nombre de** … and your surname. They will ask for your **pasaporte**. Staying two nights? *Dos noches.*';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | querer | poder | ir |
| yo | quiero | puedo | voy |
| vos | **querés** | **podés** | vas |
| él, ella | quiere | puede | va |
| nosotros | **queremos** | **podemos** | vamos |
| ellos, ustedes | quieren | pueden | van |

*e → ie* and *o → ue* everywhere except **vos** and **nosotros**. *Ir* is its own thing, and takes **a** + place (*a + el* = **al**): *voy al súper*, *voy a la facu*. **Salir** only bends in *yo*: **salgo**, *salís*, *sale*. Add an infinitive for plans: *¿Querés salir?*', title_en = 'Querer, poder, salir' where id = '78286e2b-e254-5636-a5a8-883bdf68f891' and body_md = '| | querer | poder | ir |
| yo | quiero | puedo | voy |
| vos | **querés** | **podés** | vas |
| él, ella | quiere | puede | va |
| nosotros | **queremos** | **podemos** | vamos |
| ellos | quieren | pueden | van |
*e → ie* and *o → ue* everywhere except **vos** and **nosotros**. *Ir* is its own thing, and takes **a** + place (*a + el* = **al**): *voy al súper*, *voy a la facu*. **Salir** only bends in *yo*: **salgo**, *salís*, *sale*. Add an infinitive for plans: *¿Querés salir?*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Pienso** + verb is *I plan to*: *pienso ir al cine*, *¿pensás salir hoy?* **Creo que** … is *I think that* …: *creo que está cerrado*, *¿creés que abre hoy?* And **no creo** is *I don''t think so*.', title_en = 'Pienso ir, creo que…' where id = 'eb18db97-cf2e-5687-a5df-2e4b175166b1' and body_md = 'For a film, a show or a party, ask **¿a qué hora empieza?** Porteños go out late: a **fiesta** that *empieza a las doce* is a normal Saturday, and you **volvés** at six.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Three short commands you will hear all day: *hacer* gives **hacé**, *poner* gives **poné**, and *dar* gives **dame** — *give me*: *dame otro*. Never *haz* or *pon* — those belong to another Spanish.', title_en = 'The short ones' where id = 'dc9f86b5-115a-57f2-aeb5-e87bda316574' and body_md = 'A few commands you will hear all day: *go* is **andá**; *hacer* gives **hacé**; *dar* gives **dame** — *give me*. The same recipe makes the rest: **poné** (put), **tené** (have, hold), **decí** (say), **salí** (go out). Never *ve, haz, pon, di* — those belong to another Spanish.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'On the bondi, getting on and off carries a *te* on the end: **subite** (get on), **bajate en la esquina** (get off at the corner). And **pará** stops anyone: *¡pará, pará!* In a car, **dejar** is *to drop off*: **dejame acá**, *te dejo en la esquina*.' where id = '5c1d67c6-5ad4-5b4f-bfce-ca368b14bf65' and body_md = 'On the bondi, getting on and off carries a *te* on the end: **subite** (get on), **bajate en la esquina** (get off at the corner). And **pará** stops anyone: *¡pará, pará!*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'You can''t pay the driver in cash. You tap a **SUBE** card on the reader — on buses, the subte and trains (many now take a bank card or phone too). You load it at a kiosco or a subte station: *¿Me cargás la SUBE?* When the **saldo** runs out, load it again.' where id = 'f8d95867-18ac-54cd-a860-30ed3a2df254' and body_md = 'You can''t pay the driver in cash. You tap a **SUBE** card on the reader — on buses, the subte and trains. You load it at a kiosco or a subte station: *¿Me cargás la SUBE?* When the **saldo** runs out, load it again.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'In Buenos Aires **911** is the police and **107** is the ambulance. In the street, shout **¡ayuda!** and tell someone what to do: **llamá a la policía**, *llamá una ambulancia*. *Es urgente.*' where id = '36daec09-756b-57d1-a508-f8ba61fd0b2c' and body_md = 'In Buenos Aires **911** is the police and **107** is the ambulance. In the street, shout **¡ayuda!** and tell someone what to do: **llamá a la policía**, *llamá a una ambulancia*. *Es urgente.*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Celeste** is the light blue of the flag — for porteños a different color from *azul*: *No son azules, son celestes.* **Rosa** and **naranja** keep the *-a* for masculine too: *un pantalón rosa*, *una campera naranja*.', title_en = 'Celeste, rosa, naranja' where id = '53370f9c-ba05-5f62-b511-24a2a447f934' and body_md = 'One pair of pants is **un pantalón** — singular: *este pantalón es lindo*. *Los pantalones* works too. The same goes for **un jean**. And three colours: **celeste** is the light blue of the flag; **rosa** and **naranja** never change: *una remera rosa*, *un pantalón naranja*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Colors match their noun like any adjective: *un pantalón negro*, *una remera negra*, *zapatillas negras*. Ones ending in *-e* or a consonant only change for more than one: *verde* → **verdes**, *azul* → **azules**. The color comes after the noun.', title_en = 'Colors match the noun' where id = '14ab3922-a0da-5828-9009-788ce80ae5c3' and body_md = 'Adjectives match their noun: *remera linda*, *zapatillas lindas*. Ones ending in *-e* or a consonant only change for more than one: *verde* → **verdes**, *azul* → **azules**. **Re** in front of an adjective means *really*: *re lindo*. **Muy** is *very* — and *muy chica para Juan* is *too small for Juan*. And **chico** means *small* — and also *boy* or *girl*: *la chica de la remera verde* is *the girl in the green T-shirt*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To say how clothes fit, use **me queda**: *Esta camisa me queda bien* — *this shirt fits me well*. *Me queda chico* — *it''s too small for me*. *El vestido me queda grande* — *the dress is too big for me*.', title_en = 'Me queda bien' where id = '1f894de9-91ad-51fe-8542-9bab3593187c' and body_md = 'When you don''t know the word — or don''t need it — use **esto** (this thing here) and **eso** (that thing there). They never change: *¿Cuánto sale eso?*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To pay, you don''t say *I want to pay*: you ask them to charge you — **¿me cobrás?** The change they give back is **el vuelto**; small coins and bills are **cambio**. **Cobrar** is also *to get paid*: *¿Cuándo cobrás?* — *when do you get paid?*' where id = 'cb4863d6-1af9-5447-a5f5-2a898c771f96' and body_md = 'To pay, you don''t say *I want to pay*: you ask them to charge you — **¿me cobrás?** The change they give back is **el vuelto**; small coins and notes are **cambio**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'These verbs carry a pronoun that matches the person:
| yo | **me** levanto | **me** acuesto |
| vos | **te** levantás | **te** acostás |
| él, ella | **se** levanta | **se** acuesta |
| nosotros | **nos** levantamos | |
The pronoun goes before the verb. *Acostarse* and *almorzar* change *o → ue*, but not with vos: **me acuesto**, **almuerzo** — **te acostás**, **almorzás**. ' where id = '8eaa2931-6ddd-51a7-b8ae-6270f3bc71e8' and body_md = 'These verbs carry a pronoun that matches the person:
| yo | **me** levanto | **me** acuesto |
| vos | **te** levantás | **te** acostás |
| él, ella | **se** levanta | **se** acuesta |
| nosotros | **nos** levantamos | |
The pronoun goes before the verb. *Acostarse* and *almorzar* change *o → ue*, but not with vos: **me acuesto**, **almuerzo** — **te acostás**, **almorzás**. **Los sábados** means *on Saturdays*; **antes de** + a verb is *before*: *antes de ir a la facu*. **Una vez por semana** is *once a week*; **a veces** is *sometimes*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'With a verb, **gusta** and **encanta** stay singular, even for two activities: *Me gusta leer y cocinar.* With things they follow the thing: *Me encanta el fútbol*, *me encantan las series*. To agree: **A mí también** after a *yes*, **A mí tampoco** after a *no*. With a normal verb it''s **yo**: *No bailo.* — *Yo tampoco.*', title_en = 'Me gusta + doing something' where id = 'f255cb1b-020c-5d3c-bf67-3a14a5b0ebe8' and body_md = 'With a verb, *gusta* stays singular, even for two activities:
| Me gusta bailar. | Me gusta leer y cocinar. |
| Me encanta el fútbol. | Me encantan las series. |
Agreeing with *me gusta* or *me encanta*: **A mí también** after a *yes*, **A mí tampoco** after a *no*. With a normal verb it''s **yo**: *No bailo.* — *Yo tampoco.* **Jugar** stretches like *poder*: **juego**, but **jugás**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Waking up and getting up are two verbs: **me despierto** at seven, **me levanto** at seven-thirty. With vos the stem doesn''t change: **te despertás**. The little word follows the person: *me, te, se, nos* — and **se** again for *ellos*: **se levantan**, **se acuestan**.' where id = '63f1c92c-7c0e-5bd6-a215-09afc0414392' and body_md = 'Waking up and getting up are two verbs: **me despierto** at seven, **me levanto** at seven-thirty. The little word follows the person: *me, te, se, nos* — and **se** again for *ellos*: **se levantan**, **se acuestan**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To say *the black one*, drop the noun and keep **el** or **la**: *¿El negro o el azul?* — *the black one or the blue one?* *Quiero la roja* — *I want the red one*. The same works with *este* and *ese*: *Quiero este* — *I want this one*.', title_en = 'The black one' where id = '7125b8a8-aecd-5bd7-a7f1-20cf7ffc06fb' and body_md = '| | this | that |
| masculine | **este**, **estos** | **ese**, **esos** |
| feminine | **esta**, **estas** | **esa**, **esas** |
Drop the noun and keep *el* or *la*: *¿El negro o el azul?* — *the black one or the blue one?*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The thing liked is the subject; the pronoun says who likes it:
| a mí | **me** gusta nadar | **me** interesa el tenis |
| a vos | **te** gusta viajar | **te** interesan los deportes |
| a él, a ella | **le** gusta cantar | **le** interesa la música |
| a nosotros | **nos** gusta pasear | **nos** encanta la playa |
| a ellos, a ustedes | **les** gusta el fútbol | **les** encantan las series |
With a verb it stays singular: *me gusta nadar y cantar*. To name the person, put **a** in front and keep **le**: *A mi hermano le gusta nadar.* **Odiar** is a normal verb: *odio, odiás*.' where id = '66c19e01-5dde-5df7-b8e7-53568768b420' and body_md = 'The thing liked is the subject; the pronoun says who likes it:
| a mí | **me** gusta nadar | **me** interesa el tenis |
| a vos | **te** gusta viajar | **te** interesan los deportes |
| a él, a ella | **le** gusta cantar | **le** interesa la música |
| a nosotros | **nos** gusta pasear | **nos** encanta la playa |
| a ellos | **les** gusta el fútbol | **les** encantan las series |
With a verb it stays singular: *me gusta nadar y cantar*. To name the person, put **a** in front and keep **le**: *A mi hermano le gusta nadar.* **Odiar** is a normal verb: *odio, odiás*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For a local number you buy a **chip** — a SIM card — at a phone shop or a kiosco (take your passport: they may ask for it), and then you load **datos**: *cargar datos*, the same verb as loading the SUBE. *No tengo datos* means no internet until the next wifi.' where id = 'a807dff0-189b-5406-b3c0-73d7d4b65c1f' and body_md = 'For a local number you buy a **chip** — a SIM card — at a phone shop or a kiosco, and then you load **datos**: *cargar datos*, the same verb as loading the SUBE. *No tengo datos* means no internet until the next wifi.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Hace calor**, **hace frío** — it''s hot, it''s cold. But **hay sol**, **hay viento**, **está nublado**, and **llueve** alone (for right now you''ll also hear *está lloviendo*). You yourself **tenés frío**. Seasons are flipped: *el verano* runs from late December to March. **Bárbaro** means *great*, not barbaric: *¡Bárbaro!* — Great! *Hay un sol bárbaro* — it''s really sunny.' where id = 'd48b1ff9-881c-5010-bbf2-fd3a16bc7729' and body_md = '**Hace calor**, **hace frío** — it''s hot, it''s cold. But **hay sol**, **hay viento**, **está nublado**, and **llueve** alone (for right now you''ll also hear *está lloviendo*). You yourself **tenés frío**. Seasons are flipped: *el verano* runs from late December to March.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Months have no capital: **en marzo**, **en diciembre**. Temperature is **grados**: *hace treinta grados* is a normal January day, and porteños blame everything on **la humedad**. Argentina uses Celsius: *35 grados* is very hot (95°F), and *1 grado* is almost freezing. With **desde** or **hace** + a time, Spanish uses the present: *vivo acá hace dos meses* — I''ve been living here for two months.' where id = 'f30ace7e-6e7e-53a8-8879-9f8494a8c3ef' and body_md = 'Months have no capital: **en marzo**, **en diciembre**. Temperature is **grados**: *hace treinta y cinco grados* is a normal January day, and porteños blame everything on **la humedad**. Argentina uses Celsius: *35 grados* is very hot (95°F), and *1 grado* is almost freezing.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Nobody says *cumpleaños* in a hurry: it''s **el cumple** — *¡Feliz cumple!* The verb is **cumplir**, to turn an age: *¿Cuántos años cumplís?* — *Cumplo treinta.* And *cumplís años el domingo* means your birthday is on Sunday.', title_en = 'El cumple' where id = '9bbe1671-a5b2-58f1-8923-ddd7c5e66973' and body_md = 'Nobody says *cumpleaños* in a hurry: it''s **el cumple**. For plans, **ir a** + a verb: *el sábado vamos a hacer el cumple de Juan* — and **pasado mañana** is *the day after tomorrow*. The verb is **cumplir**: *¿Cuántos años cumplís?* — *Cumplo treinta.*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For plans, use **ir a** + a verb: *Vamos a organizar el cumple.* *¿Quién va a preparar el café?* A little word like *te* or *me* goes before it: **te voy a esperar**, *¿me vas a ayudar?* You will also hear *voy a esperarte*.', title_en = 'Voy a + verb' where id = 'd848ca5a-83f6-5ef0-82e0-4395a0511149' and body_md = 'With two verbs, the little word goes before the first one or on the end of the second — never in between: **te voy a esperar** = **voy a esperarte**; **¿me vas a ayudar?** = **¿vas a ayudarme?** Porteños mostly put it first.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'English *bring* is two verbs here. **Llevar** is to a place where you are not yet: *¿Qué llevo al asado?* **Traer** is to the place where you are now: *¿Podés traer hielo?* Going to a friend''s place, always ask **¿qué llevo?**', title_en = 'Llevar or traer' where id = 'd5a4acc0-9d64-5970-8f68-5d4ed9936d96' and body_md = '**Estoy laburando** — I''m working (right now). In Argentina, *estoy llegando* can mean you''re still ten minutes away.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**La semana que viene** is *next week* — the week that comes. Same with days: *el viernes que viene*. **El próximo viernes** means the same. **La próxima** alone is *next time*: *La próxima invito yo.*', title_en = 'La semana que viene' where id = '54719e83-d9d7-5d73-98e3-8ba760627cc8' and body_md = '**Ir a** + infinitive talks about plans: *Vamos a hacer un asado.* **La semana que viene** is *next week*. Same with days: *el viernes que viene*. **El próximo viernes** means the same.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Boludo** is common between close friends and an insult to anyone else — say it only to friends you know well. **Quilombo** means a mess; it''s informal, not rude, but keep it out of formal settings.' where id = '01e1a3a8-575e-5121-9fc4-7dd8f47262c1' and body_md = '**Boludo** is common between close friends and an insult to anyone else — understand it, don''t use it yet. **Quilombo** means a mess; it''s informal, not rude, but keep it out of formal settings.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Tell your life story with the past you already know: **nací** (*I was born*), **viví**, **volví**. **Me crié** is *I grew up*, and it always takes **me**: *Nací en Italia, pero me crié en Buenos Aires.* To ask: *¿Te criaste acá?*', title_en = 'Your story: nací, me crié, viví' where id = 'ef4a4d49-d272-5947-9455-4f31401357f9' and body_md = '**Nací**, **viví**, **volví** — the -er and -ir past you already know tells a whole life. For *ellos* it ends in **-ieron**: *mis viejos **vivieron** en Brasil*, ***salieron** temprano*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | hacer | ver | decir | venir | poder |
| yo | hice | vi | dije | vine | pude |
| vos | hiciste | viste | dijiste | viniste | pudiste |
| él, ella | hizo | vio | dijo | vino | pudo |
| nosotros | hicimos | vimos | | | |
A new stem, then *-e, -iste, -o*, with no accent — *hizo* is spelled with a *z*. *Ver* keeps it short: *vi, viste, vio*.', title_en = 'The irregular past' where id = '318d0b7a-680c-503c-9bd5-22439af48493' and body_md = '| | hacer | ver | decir | venir | poder |
| yo | hice | vi | dije | vine | pude |
| vos | hiciste | viste | dijiste | viniste | pudiste |
| él, ella | hizo | vio | dijo | vino | pudo |
| nosotros | hicimos | vimos | | | |
A new stem, then *-e, -iste, -o*, with no accent — *hizo* is spelled with a *z*. *Ver* keeps it short: *vi, viste, vio*. Tell the story in order with **primero**, **entonces**, **al final**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Cenamos** and **salimos** look the same in the present and the past: *we have dinner* or *we had dinner*, *we go out* or *we went out*. Only -ar and -ir verbs do this; -er verbs change: **comemos** (now), **comimos** (then). A porteño never gets lost: **anoche**, **ayer**, **el sábado** — the time word does the work.' where id = '9f2c679d-71d9-54c9-8c34-e6bc1cf22a1b' and body_md = '**Cenamos** and **salimos** look the same in the present and the past: *we have dinner* or *we had dinner*, *we go out* or *we went out*. A porteño never gets lost: **anoche**, **ayer**, **el sábado** — the time word does the work.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Cené, cenaste, cenó, cenamos, cenaron**; **viví, viviste, vivió, vivimos, vivieron**. Two sets of endings, and every regular verb takes one of them: -ar verbs go like *cenar*; -er and -ir verbs go like *vivir*.' where id = '22eec0b9-282c-5b1e-a1da-ffdac83fdbc5' and body_md = '**Cené, cenaste, cenó, cenamos, cenaron**; **viví, viviste, vivió, vivimos, vivieron**. Two sets of endings, and every regular verb takes one of them.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Two more with their own stem and no accent: **traje, trajiste, trajo** (brought) and **quise, quisiste, quiso** (wanted, tried). **Quise** is about one moment: *I wanted to* (and tried). **No quise**: *I didn''t want to* (and didn''t). **Quise venir, pero no pude** — *I wanted to come but couldn''t* — is the porteño apology for a missed asado.' where id = '38bd929f-9d15-5f91-9679-cd20e1ac26fb' and body_md = 'Two more with their own stem and no accent: **traje, trajiste, trajo** (brought) and **quise, quisiste, quiso** (wanted, tried). **Quise** is about one moment — *I tried to*; **no quise** — *I refused*. **Quise venir, pero no pude** — *I wanted to come but couldn''t* — is the porteño apology for a missed asado.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| more than | **más** alto **que** yo |
| less than | **menos** caro **que** |
| as … as | **tan** lindo **como** |
| better, worse | **mejor**, **peor** |
| older, younger | **más grande**, **más chico** |
| really | rico → **riquísimo**, caro → **carísimo** |
The describing word still matches the person: *mi hermana es más alta que yo*. Say **mejor** for *better*; about a person, **más buena** means *nicer*. **El más chico** is *the youngest*, **el peor** *the worst*.' where id = '8413be7f-d993-58d5-87be-fbc6a78cbf25' and body_md = '| more than | **más** alto **que** yo |
| less than | **menos** caro **que** |
| as … as | **tan** lindo **como** |
| better, worse | **mejor**, **peor** |
| older, younger | **más grande**, **más chico** |
| really | rico → **riquísimo**, caro → **carísimo** |
The describing word still matches the person: *mi hermana es más alta que yo*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| him, or a masculine thing | **lo**, **los** | ¿El audio? **Lo** mando ahora. |
| her, or a feminine thing | **la**, **las** | ¿La tarjeta? **La** tengo. |
| to him, her, them | **le**, **les** | **Le** doy la llave. |
| me, you, us | **me**, **te**, **nos** | **Te** llamo mañana. |
Before a normal verb: *la tengo*. With a name you often say both: *lo llamo a Juan*, *les mando un audio a mis viejos*. Stuck to the end of a command, with no accent: **llamame**, **dame**, **mandame**, **prestame**. **Buscar** is *to look for*, and also *to pick someone up*: *te busco a las ocho* = *te paso a buscar*.' where id = '863cc68c-e7da-5e85-9141-6c897afcf44b' and body_md = '| him, or a masculine thing | **lo**, **los** | ¿El audio? **Lo** mando ahora. |
| her, or a feminine thing | **la**, **las** | ¿La tarjeta? **La** tengo. |
| to him, her, them | **le**, **les** | **Le** doy la llave. |
| me, you, us | **me**, **te**, **nos** | **Te** llamo mañana. |
Before a normal verb: *la tengo*. With a name you often say both: *lo llamo a Juan*, *les mando un audio a mis viejos*. Stuck to the end of a command, with no accent: **llamame**, **dame**, **mandame**, **prestame**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Even when you name the person, the **le** stays: **le dije a Juan que no**, **le di la llave a Sofi**, **les mandé las fotos a mis viejos**. English says it once; a porteño says it twice. With *lo* or *la* next to it, *le* turns into **se**: *¿La foto? Ya se la mandé a Juan.*', title_en = 'Le di la llave a Sofi' where id = '89462fe8-f55c-5371-aa23-378aa233d61a' and body_md = 'Even when you name the person, the **le** stays: **le dije a Juan que no**, **le di la llave a Sofi**, **les mandé las fotos a mis viejos**. English says it once; a porteño says it twice. And a message is not *received*, it *reaches* you: **¿Te llegó mi audio?** — **Sí, me llegó.**';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Dar** has a short past with no accents: **di, diste, dio** — *le di la llave*. And *buscar* bends in *yo* to keep the hard *c* sound: **busqué** (not *buscé*). **Buscar** is *to look for* and also *to pick someone up*: *busqué la billetera*, *la busqué a Mica en la estación*.' where id = '7fd0a81b-3973-5a9c-8a43-62a122aa7461' and body_md = '**Dar** has a short past with no accents: **di, diste, dio** — *le di la llave*. And *buscar* bends in *yo* to keep the hard *c* sound: **busqué** (not *buscé*).';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Clothes go in the **lavarropas**; to **planchar** them is optional for most porteños. The floor: **barrer** with the **escoba**, then you **pasás el trapo** — the wet *trapo de piso*.' where id = 'aff1bd39-fd35-5a50-a00c-5f4e71e503d4' and body_md = 'Clothes go in the **lavarropas**; to **planchar** them is optional for most porteños. The floor: **barrer** with the **escoba**, then a wet **trapo** — *el trapo de piso*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For where you went, porteños mostly say **fui a** or **me fui a**: *me fui a Bariloche*, *¿adónde te fuiste en enero?* **Viajar** is more about the trip itself: *viajé en micro*, *viajé sola*, *viajo mañana*. *Viajé a Bariloche* is fine too, just less everyday.' where id = '5877b8a4-6b4d-5004-858e-e0b6d30d2243' and body_md = 'For where you went, porteños say **fui a** or **me fui a**: *me fui a Bariloche*, *¿adónde te fuiste en enero?* **Viajar** is for the trip itself: *viajé en micro*, *viajé sola*, *viajo mañana*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Porteños go on **vacaciones** in January and February, and *la costa* — Mar del Plata, Pinamar — is where half of Buenos Aires ends up. A small detail: **y** turns into **e** before an *i* sound — *fuimos a la montaña e hizo mucho frío*.', title_en = 'January, and e for y' where id = 'bd699582-34b8-5eff-8b28-4010c536d54e' and body_md = 'Porteños go on **vacaciones** in January and February, and *la costa* — Mar del Plata, Pinamar — is where half of Buenos Aires ends up.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For a porteño **la costa** is the Atlantic beaches south of the city, where you rent a **carpa** — a beach tent by the day. The other classic is **las sierras** of Córdoba: a **río** instead of the sea. A **carpa** is also a normal camping tent: *me fui al río con la carpa*.' where id = '3e0c5f85-ecd5-5ae1-8b4e-81aea77a6ddc' and body_md = 'For a porteño **la costa** is the Atlantic beaches south of the city, where you rent a **carpa** — a beach tent by the day. The other classic is **las sierras** of Córdoba: a **río** instead of the sea.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Contame** opens it; **de repente** is the twist, **por suerte** the relief, **al final** the end. **Igual** is *anyway*, *still*: *estoy cansada, pero igual voy*. **O sea** is *I mean* or *so*. **¿Qué contás?** is just a greeting: *what''s new?*' where id = 'c3ebca78-c01d-5635-ae32-235914cc3de0' and body_md = '**Contame** opens it; **de repente** is the twist, **por suerte** the relief, **al final** the end. **Igual** — *anyway* — goes almost anywhere, and **o sea** is *I mean* or *so*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | ser | tener | vivir | ir |
| yo, él, ella | era | tenía | vivía | iba |
| vos | eras | tenías | vivías | ibas |
| nosotros | éramos | teníamos | vivíamos | íbamos |
This past describes: how things *were*, what you *had*, where you *lived*, what you *used to* do. *Yo* and *él* share one form — the story tells you which. **De chico** is *as a kid*: **De chico vivía en Rosario.** It changes with the person: **de chica** (a woman), **de chicos** (*we*).' where id = '862e703e-1590-5d4a-9240-1b3e1a058369' and body_md = '| | ser | tener | vivir | ir |
| yo, él, ella | era | tenía | vivía | iba |
| vos | eras | tenías | vivías | ibas |
| nosotros | éramos | | | íbamos |
This past describes: how things *were*, what you *had*, where you *lived*, what you *used to* do. *Yo* and *él* share one form — the story tells you which. **De chico** is *as a kid*: **De chico vivía en Rosario.** It changes with the person: **de chica** (a woman), **de chicos** (*we*).';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Wanting and being able are states, so back then they take the imperfect: **De chico quería ser maestro** — *as a kid I wanted to be a teacher*; **no podía salir solo** — *I wasn''t allowed out on my own*. **En esa época** — *back then* — sets the whole scene. At a counter, **quería un cortado** is just a polite *I''d like a cortado*. With a person, **querer a** is *to love*: *quería mucho a mi maestra*.' where id = 'a54ef42c-739f-54d1-8ea1-e7c82fed10f9' and body_md = 'Wanting and being able are states, so back then they take the imperfect: **De chico quería ser maestro** — *as a kid I wanted to be a teacher*; **no podía salir solo** — *I wasn''t allowed out on my own*. **En esa época** — *back then* — sets the whole scene. At a counter, **quería un cortado** is just a polite *I''d like a cortado*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'School here is **la primaria** (six to twelve) and then **la secundaria**. In a state primary school everyone wears a white **guardapolvo** over their clothes, and the best part of the day is the **recreo**. In primaria the teacher is **la maestra** or **el maestro**; from secundaria on it is **el profesor**, **la profe**. Each year of primaria is a **grado**: *primer grado*.' where id = 'a4adbfa9-faf6-51e4-b4d1-cd956aff9126' and body_md = 'School here is **la primaria** (six to twelve) and then **la secundaria**. In a state school everyone wears a white **guardapolvo** over their clothes, and the best part of the day is the **recreo**. In primaria the teacher is **la maestra** or **el maestro**; from secundaria on it is **el profesor**, **la profe**. Each year of primaria is a **grado**: *primer grado*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'In the past, *gustar* and *encantar* work like any -ar verb: **me gustaba**, **me encantaba** — *I liked*, *I loved*. Several things take an **-n**: **me gustaban los dibujitos**. The same **-n** makes the *they* form of any verb: **los pibes jugaban a la pelota en la vereda**.' where id = '9ec733ad-4e25-5b19-b479-b8f53e3f3e70' and body_md = 'In the past, *gustar* and *encantar* work like any -ar verb: **me gustaba**, **me encantaba** — *I liked*, *I loved*. Several things take an **-n**: **me gustaban los dibujitos**. *Ellos* too: **los pibes jugaban a la pelota en la vereda**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A fan is **un hincha** or **una hincha**: the word is the same for a man or a woman. Say who you support with **ser hincha de**: *Mi papá es re hincha de la selección* — my dad is a huge fan of the national team.' where id = 'b8f8cc97-9d17-54ae-ac0a-deffbff54047' and body_md = 'A fan is a **hincha**, and a **gol** is shouted, not said.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Scores are said with **a**: **ganamos dos a uno**, *empatamos cero a cero*. To score is **hacer un gol**: *Juan hizo dos goles*. And the field — and the whole stadium — is **la cancha**.' where id = '92fc2db4-2843-50a2-aab4-fa03169e8b02' and body_md = 'Scores are said with **a**: **ganamos dos a uno**, *empatamos cero a cero*. To score is **hacer un gol**: *Juan hizo dos goles*. And the pitch — and the whole stadium — is **la cancha**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A **final** that ends in a tie goes to the **alargue** — *extra time* — and then to **penales**: the **arquero atajó** one and somebody **metió** the last. **Salir campeón** is *to win the title*. **¡Aguante!** shows love for your team, win or lose: *¡Aguante Argentina!*' where id = '0543a4d4-e086-5583-a92b-a63cb2d2b3c0' and body_md = 'A **final** that ends in a tie goes first to the **alargue** — *extra time* — and then to **penales**: the **arquero atajó** one, somebody **metió** the last, and the whole city is out in the street in the **camiseta**. A great goal is a **golazo**. **Salir campeón** is *to win the title*; **¿cómo salieron?** asks how the game ended. What you shout: **¡Vamos, Argentina!** and **¡Aguante!** with your team: *¡Aguante Boca!* And a referee who gets everything wrong **no pega una**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The other team is *they*: **ganaron**, **perdieron**, **empataron**. Yours is usually *we*, from the bar or the sofa: **¡salimos campeones!** About your own team you can say either: **ganamos** (we, the fans) or **ganaron** (they, the players).' where id = 'aefc05cf-1bc3-5355-80ac-66c5469787aa' and body_md = 'The other team is *they*: **ganaron**, **perdieron**, **empataron**. Yours is usually *we*, from the bar or the sofa: **¡salimos campeones!** You can still say **juegan** or **ganaron** about the players.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'After a game it''s **ganamos**, **perdimos** or **empatamos** — *we* won, even if you were on the sofa. Fans always talk as part of the team: *Anoche ganamos tres a uno.*' where id = '7fe05051-cb0d-51d1-a483-3d0d35b01aa0' and body_md = 'After a match it''s **ganamos**, **perdimos** or **empatamos** — *we* won, even if you were on the sofa. The first football question you will get in Argentina: **¿De qué equipo sos?** — **Soy de Boca.** **Soy de River.** Which one, the course leaves to you.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The tip is **la propina**, usually 10 percent and in cash. The bill may also have a small charge per person, the *cubierto*: it is not the tip. **¿Compartimos?** — *shall we share?* — is how two people order one enormous *bife*.' where id = '2910b1f9-2188-52b3-b99b-5ff32f745b64' and body_md = 'The tip is **la propina**, usually 10 percent and in cash. **¿Compartimos?** — *shall we share?* — is how two people order one enormous *bife*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A bife comes jugoso, a punto, or **bien cocido** — *well done*; **vuelta y vuelta** is seared on each side and almost raw inside. The bill has a line for the **cubierto** — *the cover charge*: the bread and the cutlery.' where id = 'd9075515-9557-5e2e-986b-a39b62161f51' and body_md = 'A bife comes jugoso, a punto, or **bien cocido** — *well done*; **vuelta y vuelta** is barely warm. The bill has a line for the **cubierto** — *the cover charge*: the bread and the cutlery.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Traditions told from back then are imperfect: **nos juntábamos**, **festejábamos**, **armábamos el arbolito** on the 8th of December. **Es costumbre…** — *it''s the custom to…* — brings them into the present: *Es costumbre juntarnos en Navidad.*' where id = 'a080f44e-07bb-51f5-922b-1fe5cf6548e6' and body_md = 'Traditions told from back then are imperfect: **nos juntábamos**, **festejábamos**, **armábamos el arbolito** on the 8th of December. **Tenemos la costumbre de…** — *we have the custom of…* — brings them into the present.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The first question in a new friendship. A team is a **cuadro**, and you inherit it: *Soy de Independiente, el cuadro de mi abuelo.* Answer with **soy de** or **soy hincha de**. **Hinchar por** is for one game or the national team: *Hincho por la selección.*' where id = 'bb6b163b-1fc3-54dd-91e3-016a0d3e09ba' and body_md = 'The first question in a new friendship. A team is a **cuadro**, and you don''t choose it, you inherit it: **soy del mismo cuadro que mi viejo**. The answer is **soy de** or **soy hincha de**: *Soy de Racing.* *Soy hincha de River.* **Hinchar por** is for one game or the national team: **¿por quién hinchás?** — *Hincho por Argentina.*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Boca** against **River** is **el superclásico**; any other big rivalry game is a **clásico**. Boca fans are called *bosteros* and River fans *gallinas*: they say it about themselves with pride, but from you it can be an insult. Which side you''re on, the course leaves to you.' where id = '8f4c23b2-5684-59ec-a311-4cb9e59ce5a6' and body_md = 'The two biggest teams, **Boca** and **River**, playing each other is **el superclásico**; any derby is a **clásico** — *Racing* against *Independiente*, for one. Boca fans are called *bosteros* and River fans *gallinas*: insults they now wear with pride. The fans stand on the **tribuna**. Which side you''re on, the course leaves to you.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To go to **la cancha** you are usually a **socio** — *a member* — of the **club**, and you pay a monthly fee. The **popular** is the cheap standing section, where the **hinchada** sings its **cantitos** for ninety minutes under the **banderas**.' where id = 'bcc20295-b0f0-5657-8bba-544e8abc8f78' and body_md = 'To go to **la cancha** — *estadio* is for signs and maps — you are usually **socio** — *a member* — of the **club**, and pay the cuota. Tickets are *entradas*: the **popular** is the cheap standing end, the **platea** the seats. The **hinchada** sings its **cantitos** for ninety minutes, under the **banderas**. Away fans? Mostly banned since 2013: you usually only go **de visitante** on TV.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Meat comes **jugosa** — *rare* — **a punto** — *medium* — or well done. The **parrilla** is both the grill and the restaurant.' where id = '95e185c4-bc0b-5a6f-aaf0-369094e37060' and body_md = 'Meat comes **jugosa** — *pink, juicy* — **a punto** — *medium* — or well done. The **parrilla** is both the grill and the restaurant.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Pedimos** keeps the *e*; **pidió** and **pidieron** turn it into *i*. **¿Qué pidieron?** — **Una grande de muzza y una provoleta para compartir.**' where id = '9ca4eeb2-2fba-5a4a-bc62-2e939d24aea0' and body_md = '**Pedimos** keeps the *e*; **pidió** and **pidieron** turn it into *i*. **¿Qué pidieron?** — **Una grande de muzza y dos porciones de provoleta**... and someone always asks **¿es picante?**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Porteños talk about the future with **ir a**: **voy a laburar**, **vamos a comer**. For a fixed plan the plain present works too: **viajamos el viernes**. *Viajamos* is also *we traveled*: the time word tells you which. *Next week* is **la semana que viene**, *next year* **el año que viene**.' where id = 'a5a666cc-13f5-582b-a31d-e3454f6aea44' and body_md = 'Porteños talk about the future with **ir a**: **voy a laburar**, **vamos a comer**. For a fixed plan the plain present works too: **viajamos el viernes**. *Next week* is **la semana que viene**, *next year* **el año que viene**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Tengo ganas de ir a la playa** — *I feel like going to the beach*. **Pienso ir** — *I''m planning to go*. Careful: **pensar** + a verb is *to plan to*, but **pensar que** is *to think that*: *pienso que tenés razón*.', title_en = 'Tengo ganas, pienso ir' where id = '40e8fd4a-7fef-5c78-a666-03e64f6b1eed' and body_md = '**Tengo ganas de ir a la playa** — *I feel like going to the beach*. **Pienso ir** — *I''m planning to go*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me mudé** — *I moved (house)*; **nos mudamos** — *we moved*. It always carries *me/te/se/nos*: **te mudaste**, **se mudó**. **Mudarse con** is *to move in with*. The **mudanza** is the move itself, and always a *quilombo* (a mess).' where id = '72734c3b-aa10-5b4c-819d-56584b23250e' and body_md = '**Me mudé** — *I moved (house)*; **nos mudamos** — *we moved*. The **mudanza** is the move itself, and always a *quilombo* (a mess).';
update public.tips set body_md = 'You rent through an **inmobiliaria** or straight from the **dueño**. Every month you pay the **alquiler** plus the **expensas** — *the building fees*. To sign the **contrato** you leave a **depósito** and show a **garantía**: someone who answers for you if you don''t pay.', title_en = 'Renting a place' where id = 'dbad321f-4d32-5c2e-9458-5dbbd5e6decf' and body_md = 'You rent through an **inmobiliaria** or straight from the **dueño**, and pay the **alquiler** every month. On top of the rent come the **expensas** — *the building fees* — and to move in you leave a **depósito**. A **flete** takes the **muebles** and the **colchón**, and before unpacking, **pintamos**. And *they moved* is **se mudaron**. The dream is the **casa propia** — *a place of your own*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The moment a feeling hit, or a thing slipped your mind, is preterite with its pronoun: **me sentí re mal**, **me olvidé de avisarte** (a thing you left behind takes no *de*: **me olvidé las llaves**), **nos pusimos contentos**.' where id = 'dff327fb-93ad-5ef0-b87d-b0b8f5748f57' and body_md = 'The moment a feeling hit, or a thing slipped your mind, is preterite with its pronoun: **me sentí re mal**, **me olvidé de avisarte**, **nos pusimos contentos**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The city is **la Capital** — often with no article: *vivo en Capital*. The ring of towns around it is **el conurbano**. Palermo, **San Telmo** and **La Boca** are barrios of the Capital: *Palermo está lleno de bares*, *La Boca es re turística*. The first question to any porteño: **¿en qué barrio vivís?**' where id = '9b2c23e3-838a-574f-affd-f711c01a05fe' and body_md = 'The city is **la Capital**; the ring of towns around it, in the province, is **el conurbano**. Palermo, San Telmo and La Boca are all barrios of the Capital. Each barrio has its thing: **Palermo está lleno de bares**, **en San Telmo hay una feria los domingos**, **La Boca es re turística**. The first question to any porteño: **¿en qué barrio vivís?**';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Zona norte** — the suburbs north of the General Paz, like San Isidro and Tigre — has a name for money and **árboles**; **zona sur** — Avellaneda, Lanús, Quilmes — is, in general, cheaper. Inside the Capital, Recoleta and Belgrano are the leafy north; Caballito, Almagro and Villa Crespo sit in the middle.' where id = 'ef2f7720-75af-506a-a7fb-1581bde273b9' and body_md = '**Zona norte** — the suburbs north of the General Paz, like Vicente López, San Isidro and Tigre — has the money and the **árboles**; **zona sur** — the suburbs to the south, like Avellaneda, Lanús and Quilmes — is cheaper. Inside the Capital, Recoleta and Belgrano are the leafy north; Caballito, Almagro and Villa Crespo sit in the middle.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Remember **queda** for where a place *is*: **¿dónde queda Palermo?** New here is **me parece** — *I think, it seems to me*: *me parece re caro*. To ask for an opinion: **¿qué te parece el depto?** — *what do you think of the apartment?*', title_en = 'Queda, me parece' where id = 'f7ca6bf1-8ae1-516b-935e-ab0b2f6dcb07' and body_md = 'For where a place *is*, porteños say **queda**: **¿dónde queda la farmacia?** — *where''s the pharmacy?* — and **me queda cerca** — *it''s close to me*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'You know **queda** and **quedan** for where places are. Put the person in front to say how far it is *for them*: **¿te queda cerca la facu?** — *is college close for you?* — *el centro te queda cerca*.', title_en = 'Te queda' where id = 'ca47c7e9-05d9-5bfa-9df1-7a8c4223003a' and body_md = 'Two places: **quedan** — *San Isidro y Tigre quedan en zona norte*. For you: **¿te queda cerca?** — *is it close for you?*. It''s the same *queda*, with whoever it''s for in front.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The **calesita** in the plaza, **golosinas** from the kiosco, a **barrilete** on a windy day, and the **álbum** of **figuritas** you filled for every **Mundial** — **lo llenábamos entre todos** — *we used to fill it together*.' where id = '086d52a0-b9ba-519c-bd38-ddf31a31c648' and body_md = 'The **calesita** in the plaza, **golosinas** from the kiosco, a **barrilete** on a windy day, and the **álbum** of **figuritas** you filled for every **Mundial** — **lo llenábamos entre todos**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'With a vos command the pronoun joins the end: **ayudame**, **alcanzame** — *help me*, *hand me*. No written accent: the stress stays on **-da-** and **-za-**, so not *ayúdame*.' where id = '0a0c6336-f327-5f98-83ba-2d0a95f6e002' and body_md = 'With a vos command the pronoun joins the end: **ayudame**, **alcanzame** — *help me*, *hand me*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Still a plain question in the present with **me** in front: **¿me acompañás?** — *will you come with me?*; **¿me llevás?** — *can you give me a ride?*; **¿me regás las plantas?** — *can you water my plants?* Asking for two of you? Swap *me* for **nos**: **¿nos llevás?** — *can you take us?*' where id = '795eda4c-1b7a-5a23-97b2-aac4263f8f38' and body_md = 'Still a plain question in the present with **me** in front: **¿me acompañás?** — *will you come with me?*; **¿me llevás?** — *can you give me a ride?*; **¿me regás las plantas?** — *can you water my plants?* Asking for two of you? Swap *me* for **nos**: **¿nos sacás una foto?**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'It works on adverbs too: **cerquita** — *close by*; **despacito** — *nice and slow*. **Chiquito** — *small, little*. Careful: **hablá más despacito** can mean *slower* or *quieter* — the situation tells you.' where id = '9c22a7d9-d890-5e17-a088-75954c74be37' and body_md = 'It works on adverbs too: **cerquita** — *close by*; **despacito** — *nice and slow*. **Chiquito** — *small, little*. Careful: **hablá más despacito** usually means *keep your voice down*, not *slow down*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Words ending in *-r*, *-n*, *-e* take **-cito**: **calor → calorcito**, **café → cafecito**. Short *sol* does too: **solcito**. Words in *-o* just swap it for **-ito**, and a *c* turns *qu*: **fresco → fresquito**; a *z* turns *c*: **pedazo → pedacito**. Porteños love diminutives for nice weather: **hace fresquito**, **qué lindo calorcito**.' where id = '25238004-814b-58f4-824a-ded9fff9bc9e' and body_md = 'Words ending in *-r*, *-n*, *-e* take **-cito**: **calor → calorcito**, **café → cafecito**. Short *sol* does too: **solcito**. Words in *-o* just swap it for **-ito**, and a *c* turns *qu*: **fresco → fresquito**. Porteños love diminutives for nice weather: **hace fresquito**, **qué lindo calorcito**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Nouns: **una cosita**, **un pedacito**, **un besito**. Adjectives: **calentito** — *nice and warm*; **cortito**; **igualito a su papá**; **solito** — *all by himself* (to an adult it sounds tender or teasing, so keep it for friends). Adverbs: **tempranito**, **rapidito**. It agrees like any adjective: **una sopa calentita**.' where id = '48fa40c1-c5f2-58f5-8669-4ba8e2da759c' and body_md = 'Nouns: **una cosita**, **un pedacito**, **un besito**. Adjectives: **calentito** — *nice and warm*; **cortito**; **igualito a su papá**; **solito** — *all by himself*. Adverbs: **tempranito**, **rapidito**. It agrees like any adjective: **una sopa calentita**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A porteño host says **pasen, pasen** at the door, **pónganse cómodos**, and **no se preocupen** when you apologize for being late. **Están en su casa** — *make yourselves at home*.' where id = '01a808b3-a1c9-5477-ae3a-bbb29595b2ee' and body_md = 'A porteño host says **pasen, pasen** at the door, **pónganse cómodos**, and **no se preocupen** when you apologize for being late.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| one person (vos) | more than one (ustedes) |
| pasá | **pasen** |
| esperá | **esperen** |
| vení | **vengan** |
| traé | **traigan** |
| sentate | **siéntense** |
| no te preocupes | **no se preocupen** |

-ar verbs end in **-en**, the rest in **-an**, built on the *yo* form: *vengo* → **vengan**, *traigo* → **traigan**. The pronoun is **se**, stuck on the end — and then the accent appears: **siéntense, quédense**. After *no* it goes in front: **no se preocupen**.' where id = 'f534bcfd-43c6-5d81-a814-89f5071f8271' and body_md = '| one person (vos) | more than one (ustedes) |
| pasá | **pasen** |
| esperá | **esperen** |
| vení | **vengan** |
| traé | **traigan** |
| sentate | **siéntense** |
| no te preocupes | **no se preocupen** |

-ar verbs end in **-en**, the rest in **-an**. The pronoun is **se**, stuck on the end — and then the accent appears: **siéntense, quédense**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| one person (vos) | more than one (ustedes) |
| probá | **prueben** |
| agarrá | **agarren** |
| tomá | **tomen** |
| no te olvides | **no se olviden** |

Also **coman**, **hagan** lugar, **vayan**, **dejen**. **Vayan** + *-ando/-iendo* is *go ahead and start*: **vayan comiendo** — *start eating*. -ar verbs **-en**, the rest **-an**. The stem is the *yo* stem: *pruebo* → **prueben**, *hago* → **hagan**, *vengo* → **vengan**. **Dejen de** + verb is *stop*: **dejen de hablar** — *stop talking*.' where id = 'a5ed425f-69c3-5b5d-816e-3fc1878a9d27' and body_md = '| one person (vos) | more than one (ustedes) |
| probá | **prueben** |
| agarrá | **agarren** |
| tomá | **tomen** |
| no te olvides | **no se olviden** |

Also **coman**, **hagan** lugar, **vayan**, **dejen**. **Vayan** + *-ando/-iendo* is *go ahead and start*: **vayan comiendo** — *start eating*. -ar verbs **-en**, the rest **-an**. The stem is the *yo* stem: *pruebo* → **prueben**, *hago* → **hagan**, *vengo* → **vengan**. The pronoun sticks on the end — **sírvanse, apúrense** — and after *no* it goes in front: **no se olviden**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¡Buen provecho!** — *enjoy!* — is said when you serve food, or when you pass people who are eating, even coworkers or strangers. The answer is **gracias**. And when the host says **sírvanse** — *help yourselves* — everybody starts right away.' where id = '1a5ebe3a-b4e7-546a-b4ed-cb9dba0344f7' and body_md = '**¡Buen provecho!** — *enjoy!* — is polite when you serve food or walk in on people eating; at home, people often just start. And when the host says **sírvanse** — *help yourselves* — everybody starts right away.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A document that has run out is **vencido**: *tengo el pasaporte vencido*. What comes next: **renovar** — *renew it*; **completar el formulario** — *fill in the form*; **hacer la cola** (or **la fila**) — *stand in line*; **firmar** — *sign*.' where id = '69d02752-e744-5eaf-b2d3-5ee433c31092' and body_md = 'A document that has run out is **vencido**: *tengo el pasaporte vencido*. You renew it (**renovar**), fill in the form — **completar el formulario**: *ya completé el formulario* —, stand in line — **hacer la cola**; you will also hear **fila** — and sign (**firmar**).';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For the **residencia** you need your **antecedentes penales** — *criminal record certificate* — with the **apostilla**, the stamp that makes a foreign paper valid here, and a **certificado de domicilio** — *proof of address*. While you wait they give you the **precaria**, a temporary permit you can already work and travel with.' where id = 'aed54cfb-0f01-532e-96bf-6fc8ed773310' and body_md = 'For the **residencia** you need your **antecedentes penales** — *criminal record* — with the **apostilla**, the stamp that makes a foreign paper valid here, and a **certificado de domicilio** — *proof of address*. While you wait they give you the **precaria**, a temporary permit you can already work and travel with.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'You know **me acuerdo** — *I remember*. The moment something comes back is the past: **¡ah, ahora me acordé!**; **¿te acordaste del pan?** — *did you remember the bread?* To remind someone, use the command: **acordate de las llaves** — *remember the keys*.', title_en = 'Me acordé, acordate' where id = 'ce04f326-dc62-5b78-b284-566e6fd63f08' and body_md = '**¿Te acordás cuando…?** opens every memory at a family asado. **Me acuerdo** — *I remember*; **no me acuerdo** — *I don''t remember*. The moment it comes back is the past: **¡ah, ahora me acordé!**; **¿te acordaste de llamar?** — *did you remember to call?*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For produce porteños often use the singular for the whole product: **la papa está cara** — *potatoes are expensive*; **un kilo de cebolla** — *a kilo of onions*. And fruit that **está verde** is *not ripe* yet (*es verde* is the color).' where id = 'a7acb74c-66af-5b76-bee7-4e80edc61c85' and body_md = 'For produce porteños often use the singular for the whole product: **la papa está cara** — *potatoes are expensive*; **un kilo de cebolla** — *a kilo of onions*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'At the **fiambrería** you buy by weight: **cien gramos de jamón**, cut in **fetas** — *slices*. The classic order is **un cuarto** — 250 grams: *un cuarto de jamón cocido*. **Jamón cocido** is plain ham; **jamón crudo** is the cured one.', title_en = 'Cien gramos, un cuarto' where id = '3d839f10-580b-59a4-ae50-d6b91d794967' and body_md = 'At the fiambrería you buy by the **gramo**: **cien gramos de jamón**, cut in **fetas** — *slices*. Milk comes by the **litro**. At the **feria**, the street market, it''s still the kilo: **medio kilo de frutillas**. The classic deli order is **un cuarto** — 250 grams: **un cuarto de jamón cocido**. **Jamón cocido** is plain ham; **jamón crudo** is the cured one.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The vendor always asks **¿algo más?** — *anything else?* You answer **nada más, gracias**, or keep going: **y un kilo de naranjas**. To ask a price, **¿cuánto sale?** is the everyday way — same as *¿cuánto cuesta?* For things sold by weight you already know **¿a cuánto está?**' where id = 'bbf8899a-9326-5028-a470-f2f170b9aab4' and body_md = 'The vendor always asks **¿algo más?** — *anything else?* You answer **nada más, gracias**, or keep going: **y un kilo de naranjas**. To ask a price, **¿cuánto sale?** is the everyday way — same as *¿cuánto cuesta?*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¿Me acompañás?** — the favor is for me; **¿nos sacás una foto?** — the favor is for us. You ask with a plain present-tense question: no *can you* needed. **¿Me podrías…?** — *could you…?* — is the more careful version.' where id = '4492bbdb-8376-566f-af0c-068e10d3456b' and body_md = '**¿Me acompañás?** — the favor is for me; **¿nos sacás una foto?** — the favor is for us. It stays a question in the present — the tone does the asking.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The card for the bus and the subte is **la SUBE**: you **cargás** it at a kiosco — the same verb as charging **el celu**, the phone (short for **celular**). *Celular* is also the phone number: *pasame tu celular* — *give me your number*.', title_en = 'El celu, la SUBE' where id = '301acde2-7437-5461-8414-6fb73db5b2cc' and body_md = 'The card for the bus and the subte is **la SUBE**, and you **cargás** it at a kiosco — the same verb as charging a phone.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me quedé sin batería** — *my battery died*, literally *I was left without battery*. A call, or the power at home, **se cortó** — *it cut out*. Without *sin*, **quedarse** is *to stay*: *¿te quedaste en casa?*', title_en = 'Me quedé sin batería' where id = '4e8246f2-31a4-5303-97f3-80f702ceb6f8' and body_md = 'The phone is **el celu** (short for *celular*). *Celular* is also the phone number: **pasame tu celular** — *give me your number*. **Me quedé sin batería** — *my battery died*; **se cortó** — *it cut out*; **mandame la ubicación** — *send me your location*. Without *sin*, **quedarse** is *to stay*: **¿te quedaste en casa?**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Tech orders are plain vos commands: **descargá la app**, **borrá las fotos**. What you already did is preterite: **la descargué**, **las borré**. Day to day people say **bajá** or **bajate** for *download*: **bajate la app, es gratis**. *Descargar* is what the screen says.' where id = '6d7c070b-81b7-58f0-b526-20ee5f75be8d' and body_md = 'Tech orders are plain vos commands: **descargá la app**, **borrá las fotos**. What you already did is preterite: **la descargué**, **las borré**. Day to day people say **bajá** or **bajate** for *download*: **bajate la app, es gratis**. *Descargá* is what the screen says.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When anything stops working, porteños say it **no anda**: *no anda el wifi*, *no me anda el celu*. A machine that fails on its own takes **se**: **se apagó** — *it switched off*; **se colgó** — *it froze*. The universal fix: **apagalo y prendelo**.', title_en = 'No anda, se apagó' where id = 'ecc14597-b02a-597b-bcbf-15a4de418dbf' and body_md = 'A machine that fails on its own takes **se** and the preterite, like **se cortó**: **se apagó** — *it switched off*; **se colgó** — *it froze*. Your friend **se quedó sin batería**? Now you know why she didn''t answer. When anything stops working, porteños say it **no anda**: **no anda el wifi**, **no me anda el celu**. The universal fix: **apagalo y prendelo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To report it you **hacés la denuncia** at the **comisaría**, or online. The **policía** rarely finds the phone; the denuncia is for the insurance. To block the line, call your phone company. In an emergency, call **911**.' where id = '65cb8068-013d-5a1a-b19f-d0c054438a29' and body_md = 'To report it you **hacés la denuncia** at the **comisaría**, or online. The **policía** rarely finds the phone; the denuncia is for the insurance and the new SIM.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **me** robaron | they robbed me |
| **te** robaron | they robbed you |
| **le** robaron a mi vieja | they robbed my mom |
| **nos** robaron la bici | they stole our bike |
| **les** robaron a mis viejos | they robbed my parents |
The verb stays *robaron*; the pronoun in front says who it was taken from.' where id = '9005c132-f729-5b6c-949f-226c4f1a2c52' and body_md = '| **me** robaron | they robbed me |
| **te** robaron | they robbed you |
| **le** robaron a mi vieja | they robbed my mom |
| **nos** robaron la bici | they stole our bike |
| **me** afanaron, **me** estafaron | they stole it, they scammed me |
The verb stays *robaron*; the pronoun in front says who it was taken from.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Among friends it''s **me afanaron** — *they stole it* (slang). It is also what you say when you were overcharged: *me afanaron con el taxi* — *the taxi overcharged me*. The **motochorro** steals from a motorbike. The confession that comes with it: **me descuidé** — *I wasn''t careful*.', title_en = 'Me afanaron' where id = '9f1b4f75-62bb-5fd3-bfb4-117dc43f4612' and body_md = 'Among friends it''s **me afanaron** — *they stole it* (slang) — with the same *they* that nobody names. It moves with the victim: **te robaron**, **le robaron a mi vieja**, **nos robaron la bici**. The **motochorro** does it from a motorbike. It is also what you say when you were overcharged: **me afanaron con el taxi** — *the taxi ripped me off*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Se permite** and **se prohíbe** are sign language. Out loud people say **se puede** / **no se puede**: *acá no se puede estacionar*; *¿se puede pagar con tarjeta?* And to ask a shop: **¿hacen envíos?** — *do you deliver?*', title_en = 'Out loud: ¿se puede?' where id = '4be9d9ea-b2f7-5b90-8382-a6108a0ffd65' and body_md = '**Se permite** and **se prohíbe** are sign language. Out loud people say **se puede** / **no se puede**: *acá no se puede estacionar*; *¿se puede pagar con tarjeta?* Other signs you''ll meet every day: **abierto / cerrado**, **no funciona** — *out of order*, **liquidación** — *sale*, **solo efectivo** — *cash only*, **cuidado con el perro**. And to ask a shop: **¿hacen envíos?** — *do you deliver?*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'On the shop door: **horario de atención** — *opening hours*; **abierto / cerrado**; **solo efectivo** — *cash only*; **no funciona** — *out of order*; **liquidación** — *sale*. In a building: **no se permiten mascotas**, **se prohíbe hacer ruido**.', title_en = 'On the door' where id = 'af4c1031-7c9c-5fb0-8d8b-5b57bb841bd4' and body_md = 'The building speaks the same way: **no se permiten mascotas**, **se prohíbe hacer ruido después de las diez**. That''s written language: out loud people say **se puede** / **no se puede**. On the shop door: **horario de atención** — and outside those hours the **local** is **cerrado**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A **secreto** stays between two people: **te guardo el secreto** — *I''ll keep your secret*. And you promise it: **no se lo digo a nadie, te lo prometo** — *I won''t tell anyone, I promise*.', title_en = 'Un secreto' where id = '54258bee-3191-56f9-842b-a737c8639654' and body_md = 'To him or her, *le lo* turns into **se lo** again: **se lo digo mañana** — *I''ll tell her tomorrow*. If it''s **un secreto**: **no se lo digo a nadie, te lo prometo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Te lo paso** is *I''ll send it to you* — a number, a photo, a file. And a loan comes back **sin falta** — *for sure* (word for word, *without fail*).' where id = 'eac9e910-201e-59a3-84b2-284e5bde2587' and body_md = '**Te lo paso** is *I''ll send it to you* — a number, a photo, a file. And a loan comes back **sin falta** — *without fail*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Working from home is **hacer home office**: English words, said with a Spanish accent. It never means the room: *hoy hago home office* — *I''m working from home today*.' where id = '62b08ac0-383b-5a9f-9f1e-da41a2458c2a' and body_md = 'Working from home is **hacer home office**, in English, and said the Spanish way.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Conseguí laburo** — *I got a job*. *Conseguir* is the verb for getting anything that took effort: a *turno*, a table, an apartment.' where id = '9cfec53b-7ae4-5c4a-9a0c-768b041ea780' and body_md = '**Conseguí laburo** — *I got a job*. *Conseguir* is the porteño verb for getting anything that took effort: a *turno*, a table, an apartment.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Twice a year, in June and December, the **aguinaldo** arrives — half a month''s extra pay. Every job *en blanco* pays it by law. A **licencia** is *paid leave* for a reason (sick, a new baby, exams). Your yearly holiday is **vacaciones**.' where id = '47214591-3206-5367-b7d5-e48af1764d9e' and body_md = 'Twice a year, in June and December, the **aguinaldo** arrives — half a month''s extra pay. Ask about it at the *entrevista*, along with the **licencia** — *paid leave* for a reason (sick, a new baby, exams). Your yearly holiday is **vacaciones**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estoy saliendo con alguien** — *I''m seeing someone*. When it ends, porteños **cortan**: **cortamos** — *we broke up*. With a name they say **con Santi cortamos** — *Santi and I broke up* — and the same for a fight: **con Sofi nos peleamos**. **Nos peleamos** is *we fight* and also *we had a fight*.', title_en = 'Salir con, cortar' where id = 'dbb9fb4d-69cd-5b88-9d73-7d35bd390442' and body_md = '**Estoy saliendo con alguien** — *I''m seeing someone*. When it ends, porteños **cortan**: **cortamos** — *we broke up*. They say **con Juan cortamos** — literally *with Juan we broke up* — for *Juan and I broke up*. A fight is **nos peleamos** — *we had a fight* — or, for them, **se pelearon**; same pattern: **con Sofi nos peleamos** — *Sofi and I had a fight*. **Nos peleamos** is the same for now and for the past: *we fight* / *we had a fight*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Alguien** is *someone*, **nadie** is *nobody* — and Spanish keeps the *no* as well: **no vino nadie**. If *nadie* comes first, drop the *no*: **nadie me dijo nada**.' where id = 'e73a1f00-3237-5fcb-a397-8dbe426556e7' and body_md = '**Alguien** is *someone*, **nadie** is *nobody* — and Spanish keeps the *no* as well: **no vino nadie**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Mi prima **se casó** el sábado. | got married |
| **Nos casamos** en marzo. | we got married |
| El bebé **nació** ayer. | was born |
| ¿Dónde **naciste**? | were you born |

**Casarse** takes its pronoun; **nacer** doesn''t. **Nos casamos** is also the present: *nos casamos en julio* — *we''re getting married in July*. The wedding is a **casamiento**, and **está embarazada** is *she''s pregnant*.', title_en = 'Se casó, nació' where id = '28e641b6-4f66-5483-81c2-859687fb0e7f' and body_md = '| Mi prima **se casó** el sábado. | got married |
| **Nos casamos** en marzo. | we got married |
| El bebé **nació** ayer. | was born |
| ¿Dónde **naciste**? | were you born |
**Casarse** takes its pronoun; **nacer** doesn''t. The wedding is a **casamiento**, and **está embarazada** is *she''s pregnant*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When someone dies, family and friends meet at the **velorio** — *the wake*. You hug the family and say **te acompaño en el sentimiento** — *I''m sorry for your loss*.', title_en = 'El velorio' where id = 'fcd34b7a-a72e-5992-8c6c-e82915d7622a' and body_md = 'Porteños get married **por civil** — *at the registry office* — and, if there is a church wedding too, with a **padrino** and a **madrina**; then the **luna de miel**. When **nació una nena** or **un nene**, you visit. At a **velorio** — *a wake* — you hug and say **te acompaño en el sentimiento**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Capaz**, **a lo mejor** and **quizás** all mean *maybe*; **seguro que** is *I bet*; **supongo que** is *I guess*. All take the plain present: **capaz está en la plaza**, **seguro que es Fede**. In Buenos Aires you will hear **capaz** much more than **quizás**.', title_en = 'Capaz, a lo mejor' where id = '6f3c143b-2af0-5c70-b9e2-7435c2b347d4' and body_md = '**¿Qué hora será?** — *I wonder what time it is*. **Será** on its own shrugs: *could be*. **Capaz**, **quizás** and **seguro que** guess with the plain present: **capaz está en la plaza**; **seguro que es Juan**. In Buenos Aires you will hear **capaz** much more than **quizás**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'This future is for wondering: **¿dónde estará?** — *I wonder where he is*. Same with **¿qué hora será?**, **¿tendrá cargador?**, **¿habrá café?**, **¿qué hará?**, **¿vendrá?**, **¿qué le pasará?** For *they*, add **n**: **¿dónde estarán?**, **¿de quién serán?** For plans, porteños say *voy a*.', title_en = 'The future of guessing' where id = 'e5afe1ea-54cb-5ae0-b179-677927fb6451' and body_md = '| ser | **será** | ¿Qué hora será? |
| estar | **estará** | Estará en el laburo. |
| tener | **tendrá** | Tendrá treinta años. |
| haber | **habrá** | Habrá mucha gente. |

For plans, porteños say *voy a*. This future is for wondering and guessing: *I wonder…*, *he''s probably…*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To state a guess, porteños mostly say **debe** + infinitive: **debe estar en el laburo** — *he must be at work*; **debe tener cuarenta**; **deben ser las ocho**; to vos, **debés estar cansado** — *you must be tired*. The future is more for the question: **¿dónde estará?**, **¿qué hora será?**' where id = '7b5302fb-5521-5119-bbb6-dfeb663b58e8' and body_md = 'To state a guess, porteños mostly say **debe** + infinitive: **debe estar en el laburo** — *he must be at work*; **debe tener cuarenta**; **deben ser las ocho**. The future is more for the question: **¿dónde estará?**, **¿qué hora será?**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A porteño **maneja** (drives) an *auto*. *Conducir* is only for forms and signs. Downtown, the **tránsito** is often **imposible**, and so is finding a place to *estacionar* (park).', title_en = 'Manejar' where id = 'bdb46568-61df-5ccc-b7d5-ca48b6e9195b' and body_md = 'A porteño **maneja** (drives) an **auto** and spends half an hour trying to **estacionar** (park). *Conducir* is only for forms and signs; *aparcar* is Spain''s.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me siento mal** — *I feel sick*; **¿cómo te sentís?** — *how do you feel?* The vowel changes with *yo*, not with *vos*: **me siento**, but **te sentís**. *Dormir* does the same: **duermo**, but **dormís**; **dormí** is the past, *I slept*. On its own, **lo siento** is *I''m sorry*.', title_en = 'Me siento' where id = '1a8b45ec-c528-5164-9c7c-bb147aad29d0' and body_md = '**Me siento mal** — *I feel sick*; **¿cómo te sentís?** — *how do you feel?* On its own, **lo siento** is *I''m sorry*. The vowel changes only when it is stressed: **me siento**, but **te sentís**. *Dormir* does the same: **duermo**, but **dormís**. In the past: **dormí** — *I slept*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'One person **ceba** — pours the water from the **termo** — and passes the mate around the **ronda**. You drink it all, through the **bombilla**, and hand it back to the **cebador**, the person who pours.' where id = '04747eea-0365-5b79-8ecf-9b0b35b85709' and body_md = 'One person **ceba** — pours the water from the **termo** — and passes the mate around the **ronda**. You drink it all, through the **bombilla**, and hand it back to the one who ceba.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When you want *someone else* to do something, the second verb changes: **quiero que vengas** — *I want you to come*. This form is the **subjunctive**. **No hace falta que** — *there''s no need to* — takes it too: *no hace falta que traigas nada*.' where id = '35a38f0f-399c-5fdb-8d3e-6e516a149e18' and body_md = 'When you want *someone else* to do something, the second verb changes: **quiero que vengas** — *I want you to come*. This form is the **subjunctive**, and *querer que* is where it starts.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Venga**, **vaya**, **haga** are both *I* and *he/she*: *quiere que venga* — *he wants me/him to come*. Context, or an added **yo** or **él**, tells you who: *quiere que vaya yo*. On its own, **que** + this form is *let him* or *tell him to*: *dale, que venga*.', title_en = 'One word for yo and él' where id = '2d43e784-4fe7-5b7a-b775-ad9457aa18f4' and body_md = '**Venga**, **vaya**, **haga** are both *I* and *he/she*: *quiere que venga* — *he wants me/him to come*. The *que* and the context tell you who.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A wish is *que* + the subjunctive: **que te vaya bien** — *good luck, hope it goes well* — is also a friendly goodbye. The answer to any wish is **gracias, igualmente** — *thanks, you too*. Afterwards you ask **¿cómo te fue?** — *how did it go?*', title_en = 'Que…: a wish' where id = '5477ef64-8dc9-564c-912e-6162a954a14d' and body_md = 'A wish is *que* + the subjunctive: **que te vaya bien** — *good luck, hope it goes well*, also a friendly goodbye; **que la pases lindo** — *have a great time*; **que tengas buen finde**. The answer to any wish is **gracias, igualmente** — *thanks, you too*. And afterwards you ask **¿cómo te fue?** — *how did it go?* **Pasarla** bien or mal is *to have a good or bad time*: **la pasé re mal**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Buena onda** is the porteño compliment for a person: easy, warm, *nice*. **Mala onda** is the opposite. **Buena onda** and **mala onda** never change: *ella es buena onda*. **Simpático** is narrower — *friendly*, pleasant to talk to — and does change: **simpática**.' where id = 'ebd8e8e5-7f3a-581d-ac16-f841077ffb75' and body_md = '**Buena onda** is the porteño compliment for a person: easy, warm, *nice*. **Mala onda** is the opposite. **Simpático** is narrower: *friendly*, pleasant to talk to. Both stay the same for everyone: *ella es buena onda*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The rules for the person who pours: **calentá el agua** in the pava — *heat the water* — but **no la hiervas**: water that **hierve** burns the yerba. **Yo cebo**, you drink. When there''s no taste left, **el mate está lavado** — *washed out* — and it''s time to change the yerba.' where id = '088111ce-f197-57ed-a80c-180b1990da3e' and body_md = 'The rules of the one who ceba: **calentá el agua** in the pava — *heat the water* — but **no la hiervas**: water that **hierve** burns the yerba. **Yo cebo**, you drink. When there''s no taste left, **el mate está lavado** — *washed out* — and it''s time to change the yerba.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Gracias por todo** — *thanks for everything*; **mil gracias** — *thanks a million*; **gracias otra vez** — *thanks again*. The thanks gets bigger, the grammar doesn''t change. You already know **un montón**: *gracias un montón*.', title_en = 'Mil gracias' where id = '85eeb729-9ee3-5ef6-a492-6eadc3ca5fdf' and body_md = '**Gracias por todo**, **mil gracias**, **gracias un montón** — the thanks gets bigger, the grammar doesn''t change. Outside the thanks it is everywhere: **un montón de** + noun is *loads of* — **hay un montón de gente**, **tengo un montón de laburo** — and **me gusta un montón**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| a habit — normal verb | not yet — subjunctive |
| Cuando **vuelvo** del laburo, tomo mate. | Cuando **vuelvas**, avisame. |
| Cuando **cobro**, pago todo. | Cuando **cobre**, te invito. |
| Cuando **empiezo** a estudiar, apago el celu. | Cuando **empieces**, contame. |

**Hasta que** and **apenas** work the same way: *esperá hasta que te llame*, *apenas sepa algo, te aviso*. ' where id = 'c2c2634b-ae53-5d15-8f38-1640fa7e99c4' and body_md = '| a habit — normal verb | not yet — subjunctive |
| Cuando **vuelvo** del laburo, tomo mate. | Cuando **vuelvas**, avisame. |
| Cuando **cobro**, pago todo. | Cuando **cobre**, te invito. |
| Cuando **empiezo** a estudiar, apago el celu. | Cuando **empieces**, contame. |

**Hasta que** and **apenas** work the same way: *esperá hasta que te llame*, *apenas sepa algo, te aviso*. The open invitation: **cuando quieras**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Wishes and the future share the form: **que te diviertas**, **ojalá que ganemos**, **cuando vuelvas**, **hasta que sepa algo**. An open choice takes it too: **lo que quieras** — *whatever you want*.' where id = 'a2b395ff-2333-5d36-83a5-22f200388a41' and body_md = 'Wishes and the future share the form: **que te diviertas**, **ojalá que ganemos**, **cuando vuelvas**, **hasta que sepa algo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Day to day an opinion starts with **para mí**: *para mí, está cerrado* — *if you ask me, it''s closed*. **Para mí que** + a normal verb is a guess: *para mí que hoy llueve*. And **no me parece que** takes the subjunctive, like *no creo que*: *no me parece que haya mucha gente*.', title_en = 'Para mí' where id = '3720e015-a831-5b88-af8b-2c4948855038' and body_md = '**¿Qué te parece?** — *what do you think?* — and the answer **me parece bien** — *sounds good* — or **me parece que no** — *I don''t think so*. **No me parece que** takes the subjunctive, like *no creo que*: *no me parece que sea caro*. Day to day an opinion starts with **para mí**: **para mí, es caro**; **para mí que no viene** — *I think he''s not coming*. And to dodge the question: **ni idea**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Te aconsejo que **lleves** efectivo. | My advice: bring cash. |
| Conviene que **tomes** el subte. | Best to take the subway. |
| Es mejor que **reserves**. | Better book ahead. |
| Es importante que **uses** la SUBE. | It''s important to use your SUBE card. |
| Es mejor que **salgamos** temprano. | We''d better leave early. |

Advice with **que** takes the subjunctive. In everyday speech the short way wins — no *que*, just the infinitive: *te conviene reservar hoy*, *te conviene tomar el subte*, *te recomiendo ir en subte*. *-ar* verbs take **e** (*llevar* → **lleves**), the rest **a** (*salgo* → **salgamos**).' where id = 'ccbc17ab-2f02-5887-84a7-3b706a5db8ec' and body_md = '| Te aconsejo que **lleves** efectivo. | My advice: bring cash. |
| Conviene que **tomes** el subte. | Best to take the subway. |
| Es mejor que **reserves**. | Better book ahead. |
| Es importante que **uses** la SUBE. | Use your SUBE card. |
| Es mejor que **salgamos** temprano. | We''d better leave early. |

Advice with **que** takes the subjunctive. In everyday speech the short way wins — no *que*, just the infinitive: *te conviene reservar hoy*, *te conviene tomar el subte*, *te recomiendo ir en subte*. *-ar* verbs take **e** (*llevar* → **lleves**), the rest **a** (*salgo* → **salgamos**).';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Novedades** is news about people and plans: **¿hay novedades de Juan?**, **todavía no hay novedades**. **Noticias** works too, and is also the news on TV; **una noticia** is one piece of news. Good news gets **¡buenísimo!**; bad news **¡qué mal!**' where id = '295c40a8-2ee4-5735-8f87-9204d04bc6a2' and body_md = 'News about people is **novedades**: **¿hay novedades de Juan?**, **todavía no hay novedades**. *Noticias* is what is on TV. Good news gets **¡buenísimo!**; bad news **¡qué mal!** or **lo siento mucho**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| ¡Qué bueno que **estés** acá! | So good you''re here! |
| Qué lástima que no **vengas**. | Shame you''re not coming. |
| Me molesta que **llegue** tarde. | It bothers me that he''s late. |

A reaction to something now or later + **que** → the subjunctive. For something that already happened, the normal past: **¡qué bueno que viniste!** **Me alegro** on its own: *I''m glad*. With more: **me alegro que** or **me alegro de que** — both are used.' where id = '9fa1891b-f569-595e-a9a2-2388d6feb5fd' and body_md = '| ¡Qué bueno que **estés** acá! | So good you''re here! |
| Qué lástima que no **vengas**. | Shame you''re not coming. |
| Me molesta que **llegue** tarde. | It bothers me that he''s late. |

A reaction to something now or later + **que** → the subjunctive. For something that already happened, the normal past: **¡qué bueno que viniste!** **Me alegro** on its own: *I''m glad*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Lunfardo is Buenos Aires slang, born in the port and the tango: **morfar** (to eat), **guita** (money), **fiaca** (laziness), **pilcha** (clothes). Friends, not job interviews. **Guita** and **fiaca** are fine in any relaxed talk; **morfar** is rougher: with people you just met, say *comer*.' where id = '3fe61f9b-3382-5a80-b860-0a7c427f3415' and body_md = 'Lunfardo is Buenos Aires slang, born in the port and the tango: **morfar** (to eat), **guita** (money), **fiaca** (laziness), **pilcha** (clothes). Friends, not job interviews.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'People get lunfardo labels: a **chanta** talks big and doesn''t deliver, a **cheto** is snobby or upper-class, and someone **piola** is cool and easy-going. **No me chamuyes** — *don''t give me that* — is the subjunctive again.' where id = '71152a01-bffa-5a60-a8d2-60677b67413e' and body_md = 'People get lunfardo labels: a **chanta** talks big and doesn''t deliver, a **cheto** is posh, and someone **piola** is cool and easy-going. **No me chamuyes** — *don''t give me that* — is the subjunctive again.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**No sabía** — *I didn''t know* — is the imperfect: a state. **Me di cuenta** — *I realized* — is the moment you finally understood. **¿Sabías que…?** opens half the gossip in Buenos Aires.' where id = '6275c34f-71c5-56f0-8a46-1c252791699f' and body_md = '**No sabía** — *I didn''t know* — is the imperfect: a state. **Me di cuenta** — *I realized* — is the moment it clicked. **¿Sabías que…?** opens half the gossip in Buenos Aires.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The porteño exit starts long before the door: **bueno, me voy yendo** — *well, I''d better get going* — and then twenty minutes of talk. On the way out, love for whoever isn''t there: **saludos a tu vieja**, **mandale saludos a Juan**. *Tu vieja* / *tu viejo* is only for friends your age; to anyone else, *saludos a tu mamá*.' where id = '17486898-58dd-5c51-8771-a3b2dfd4f7a3' and body_md = 'The porteño exit starts long before the door: **bueno, me voy yendo** — *well, I''d better get going* — and then twenty minutes of talk. On the way out, love for whoever isn''t there: **saludos a tu vieja**, **mandale saludos a Juan**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | regular | shortened |
| yo, él, ella | hablar**ía**, dejar**ía**, pedir**ía**, volver**ía** | **saldría**, **tendría**, **diría** |
| vos | ir**ías** | **tendrías**, **dirías** |
| with *me* | **me quedaría** | |

**Yo en tu lugar, hablaría con él.** Vos adds **-s**: *¿vos qué le dirías?* **Tendrías que** is advice too: *tendrías que llamarlo*.', title_en = 'Hablaría, saldría, dirías' where id = 'bacc1caa-284c-580c-9706-11d855c3ab98' and body_md = '| | regular | shortened |
| yo, él, ella | habl**aría**, dej**aría**, ped**iría**, volv**ería** | **saldría**, **tendría**, **diría** |
| vos | ir**ías** | **tendrías**, **dirías** |
| with *me* | **me quedaría** | |

**Yo en tu lugar, hablaría con él.** Vos adds **-s**: *¿vos qué le dirías?* **Tendrías que** is advice too: *tendrías que llamarlo*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Yo en tu lugar** — *in your place, if I were you* — means the same as *yo que vos*, a little more serious. The advice after it is still *would*: **yo en tu lugar, hablaría con él**, **yo me quedaría**.' where id = 'f09f8f3b-acf3-5ae9-a200-3c92a0932524' and body_md = '**Yo en tu lugar** — *in your shoes* — means the same as *yo que vos*, a little more serious. The advice after it is still *would*: **yo en tu lugar, hablaría con él**, **yo me quedaría**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Dreaming together: **si tuviéramos plata, iríamos a Bariloche** — the *we* form carries an accent, **tuviéramos**. Asking a friend: **si pudieras, ¿dónde vivirías?** — *si pudieras* is the vos form. **Ganar** is *to win* and also *to earn*: *si ganara más* — *if I earned more*.' where id = '8ea5b476-7546-5c9b-95a8-649e4b351088' and body_md = 'Dreaming together: **si tuviéramos plata, iríamos a Bariloche** — the *we* form carries an accent, **tuviéramos**. Asking a friend: **si pudieras, ¿dónde vivirías?** — *si pudieras* is the vos form.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The conditional takes the edge off a request: *¿me das una mano?* becomes **¿me darías una mano?**, *¿me ayudás?* becomes **¿me ayudarías?**. **¿Te molestaría…?** — *would you mind…?* — works like *me gustaría*. With friends the plain *¿me ayudás?* is already polite; the **-ía** form is for bigger favors or people you don''t know.' where id = '3119b315-f5ed-5147-b49a-92275496d2ce' and body_md = 'The conditional takes the edge off a request: *¿me das una mano?* becomes **¿me darías una mano?**, *¿me ayudás?* becomes **¿me ayudarías?**. **¿Te molestaría…?** — *would you mind…?* — works like *me gustaría*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Day to day porteños soften a request with **quería**: **quería un turno para mañana**, **te quería pedir algo**. **Quisiera** — *I would like* — is the formal one, for the phone or an office: **quisiera un turno**; nobody orders food with it. To ask a stranger for something, add **no** and the future: **¿no tendrás hora?** — *you wouldn''t happen to have the time?*' where id = '1d87549c-7542-53ad-8a97-9ed8aef021a6' and body_md = 'Day to day porteños soften a request with **quería**: **quería un turno para mañana**, **te quería pedir algo**. **Quisiera** — *I would like* — is the formal one, for the phone or an office: **quisiera un turno**; nobody orders food with it. To ask a stranger for something, add **no** and the future: **¿no tendrás hora?** — *you would not have the time?*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Te debo diez mil pesos** — *I owe you*; **me debés la mitad** — *you owe me half*. Friends split the bill **a medias**. A **deuda** is what you owe; if you are short, say **te pago a fin de mes** — when you get paid.' where id = '236b1e04-683a-52e4-a177-8cd11208527d' and body_md = '**Te debo mil pesos** — *I owe you*; **me debés la mitad** — *you owe me half*. Friends split the bill **a medias**, and a **deuda** between friends gets paid **a fin de mes**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'News starts with **¿escuchaste…?** or **¿te enteraste?** — *did you hear?*: *¿escuchaste lo de Pablo?* The answer is **me enteré** — *I found out*: *me enteré ayer*. A useful piece of news is **un dato**: *gracias por el dato*.', title_en = '¿Escuchaste? Me enteré' where id = '375791dd-270a-541e-90ed-5b241e5fb3d0' and body_md = '**¿Escuchaste la radio?** — the vos past, like *leíste*. And a tip from someone who knows is **un dato**: *me pasaron el dato*. Gossip opens with **¿viste que…?** — *did you hear that…?*: **¿viste que Juan renunció?**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When several people told you, or you''d rather not say who, use **me contaron que…** or **me comentaron que…**: *me contaron que te mudaste*. For one person: **Mati me comentó que renunció**. Porteño news travels by word of mouth and by *audio*, a WhatsApp voice message.', title_en = 'Me contaron' where id = '51b423d8-0511-58d0-8b45-1470af269ac1' and body_md = 'One source: **mi vieja dice que…**. Several: **me contaron que…**, **me comentaron que…** — *people told me*. Porteño news travels by word of mouth and by **audio** — a WhatsApp voice message.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Before you pass it on, ask **¿es cierto?** — *is it true?* **Cierto** changes with the noun: *la noticia es cierta*. If the answer is **es mentira** — *it''s not true* — stop there. **Lo leyó en las redes** — *she read it on social media* — is not a source.', title_en = '¿Es cierto?' where id = 'f448808c-e949-5196-9800-8ef7088251d6' and body_md = 'Before you pass it on: **¿es cierto?** — *is it true?* — or **es mentira** — *it''s not true* (word for word, *it''s a lie*). **Lo leyó en las redes** — *she read it on social media* — is not a source.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Parece que** — *it seems*, *apparently* — passes on news you are not sure of: **parece que va a llover**. *Dicen que* does the same for what people say: *dicen que va a llover todo el finde*. If it turns out to be false, **es mentira**.', title_en = 'Dicen que, parece que' where id = '60f3cec7-feb6-5d7d-87b3-4b4cee709cc5' and body_md = '**Dicen que** — *they say*, *apparently* — is how a porteño passes on anything heard second-hand. **Parece que** does the same with a shrug.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Name your source first, then the news: **lo dijeron en la radio**, **lo vi en las redes**, *lo leí en el diario*, *lo vi en la tele* — or *me llamó Sofi y me dijo que…*', title_en = '¿Viste la noticia?' where id = 'df56a42d-f2d8-562e-88b5-84ec61853925' and body_md = 'Name your source first, then the news: **Leí en el diario que…**, **lo vi en la tele** — and **me llamó Sofi y me dijo que…**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A porteño sentence breathes through its fillers: **ponele** — *let''s say*; **digamos** — *sort of*; **qué sé yo** — *I don''t know*; **bah** — *well, I mean*: *son las ocho, bah, ponele* — or a shrug, *oh well*. The ones you will hear most: **o sea** — *I mean*; **tipo** — *like, around*: *es tipo a las nueve*; and **viste** at the end, for *you know*: *estaba cansado, viste*.' where id = '6adce778-5bd3-5ead-8fc5-69d118ef84f7' and body_md = 'A porteño sentence breathes through its fillers: **ponele** — *let''s say*; **digamos** — *sort of*; **qué sé yo** — *I don''t know*; **bah** — *well, I mean*: *son las ocho, bah, ponele*. The ones you will hear most: **o sea** — *I mean*; **tipo** — *like, around*: *es tipo a las nueve*; and **viste** at the end, for *you know*: *estaba cansado, viste*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Se me** + verb says it happened *to* you, by accident — you didn''t do it on purpose: **no fue mi culpa, se me cayó** — *it wasn''t my fault, I dropped it*. And the excuse every porteño has ready when they''re late: **se me hizo tarde** — *it got late*.', title_en = 'Nobody''s fault' where id = '22f82d78-a640-5c67-b204-ef2caa3e3182' and body_md = 'That''s the whole point: **no fue mi culpa, se me cayó**. And the excuse every porteño has ready when they''re late: **se me hizo tarde**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| same person — infinitive | someone else — subjunctive |
| Estudio **para aprender**. | Te lo explico **para que entiendas**. |
| | Te lo mando **para que lo leas**. |
| | Avisame **antes de que** llegue. |

In an order, **para que** is normal even for the same person: **llevá la campera para que no tengas frío** (also right: *para no tener frío*).' where id = 'c3db5128-fa8a-560f-886b-8a3374977ee4' and body_md = '| same person — infinitive | someone else — subjunctive |
| Estudio **para aprender**. | Te lo explico **para que entiendas**. |
| | Te lo mando **para que lo leas**. |
| | Avisame **antes de que** llegue. |

When you tell someone to do something, **para que** is normal too: **llevá la campera para que no tengas frío**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Prices **suben** — or **aumentan**, same thing — and, now and then, **bajan**. **Cobrar** has two meanings. *To charge*: **¿cuánto te cobraron?** — *how much did they charge you?* And *to get paid*: **¿ya cobraste?** — *did you get paid yet?*', title_en = 'Subir, bajar, cobrar' where id = '8af67e04-9d96-5ada-98ea-78bbea30080c' and body_md = 'Prices **suben** — or **aumentan**, same thing — and, now and then, **bajan**. **¿Cuánto te cobraron?** — *how much did they charge you?* **Cobrar** is also *to get paid*: **cobro el viernes** — *I get paid on Friday*; **¿ya cobraste?** A **precio** is a price; *está a buen precio* — *it''s a good price*. When it isn''t: **es un afano** — *it''s a rip-off*; **está por las nubes** — *sky-high*; **sale un ojo de la cara** — *it costs a fortune*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'In Buenos Aires prices **aumentan** so often that it is small talk: *¿viste cómo aumentó el café?* Your **aumento** — *raise* — never keeps up with the **inflación**. When something costs too much: **está por las nubes** — *sky-high*; **sale un ojo de la cara** — *it costs a fortune*.', title_en = 'Todo aumenta' where id = 'da454431-0283-5e8b-a68d-ad8b4d5854e7' and body_md = 'In Buenos Aires prices **aumentan** so often that the word is small talk: **¿viste cómo aumentó el café?** The **aumento** of your salary never quite keeps up with the **inflación**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Crecer** is *to grow* — a city, a kid, a tree: **el barrio creció**, **crecí en Rosario** — *I grew up in Rosario*. Porteños also say **me crié**: *me crié en Flores* — *I grew up in Flores*. ' where id = '3b867a4a-8a39-52fc-bdb4-73a4c0c46453' and body_md = '**Crecer** is *to grow* — a city, a kid, a tree: **el barrio creció**, **crecí en Rosario** — *I grew up in Rosario*. Porteños also say **me crié**: *me crié en Flores* — *I grew up in Flores*. A building is an **edificio**: **hay cada vez más edificios**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Por las dudas** — *just in case*; **de última** — *if all else fails*; **si querés** — *if you like*. Say them and you sound like you''re from here.' where id = 'c2f1eb75-56ed-521b-8cf9-2a6ca57325cc' and body_md = '**Por las dudas** — *just in case*; **de última** — *if all else fails*; **en serio** — *seriously*; **si querés** — *if you like*. Say them and you sound like you''re from here.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'One past behind another: **había** + a participle. **Cuando llegué, ya habían comido** — *when I got there, they''d already eaten*. Yo, él and ella take **había**; vos, **habías**; ellos, **habían**. Pronouns go in front: **ya se había ido**, **no me habían dicho nada**. *Hecho, dicho, visto* are the irregular ones.', title_en = 'Había + -ado, -ido' where id = '1ce38771-b5cc-5d17-9f00-d8a1112042e5' and body_md = '| yo, él, ella | **había** | comido, llegado, salido |
| vos | **habías** | hecho, dicho, visto |
| ellos | **habían** | |
One past behind another: **Cuando llegué, ya habían comido** — *when I got there, they''d already eaten*. Pronouns go in front: **ya se había ido**, **no me habían dicho nada**. *Hecho, dicho, visto* are the irregular ones. Any participle goes with any person: **habías comido**, **había hecho**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Te transfiero** — *I''ll transfer it to you*; with vos, **¿me transferís?** The past: **te transferí**, **¿me transferiste?** — but él changes to **transfirió**. Asking for it: **transferime**.', title_en = 'Transferir' where id = '71a97b7b-6510-5688-b13f-983c17a2d112' and body_md = '*Transferir* changes its stem in the past for *él*: **transfirió**. With vos it doesn''t: **¿me transferiste?** Asking for it: **transferime**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The ATM is **el cajero**: **voy al cajero a sacar plata**. Paying a friend goes by **transferencia** to their **alias** — a few words instead of an account number: **¿a qué alias transferiste?** After it: **¿me mandás el comprobante?**', title_en = 'El cajero y el alias' where id = 'bf96bee5-076e-5167-adb6-ac24c4793a4d' and body_md = 'The ATM is **el cajero** — you go **a sacar plata**. Most porteños split the bill by **transferencia**: **te transfiero** — *I''ll transfer it to you*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Nobody arrives on time: **si te dicen a las nueve, llegás a las nueve y media**. In the mate round **gracias** means *no more for me*: **si decís gracias, no tomás más**. Men greet each other with a kiss too. And **la propina** is about ten per cent, in cash.' where id = 'c7048a9e-3730-5fc1-bced-2284e967b9c4' and body_md = 'Nobody arrives on time: **si te dicen a las nueve, llegás nueve y media**. In the mate round **gracias** means *no more for me*: **si decís gracias, no tomás más**. Men greet each other with a kiss too. And **la propina** is about ten per cent, in cash.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When the meat reaches the table, **se aplaude al asador**: *¡un aplauso para el asador!* **Se brinda** with everyone at the table. Leaving without saying goodbye to each person? Very **maleducado**. And **los ñoquis del 29**: on the 29th of each month people eat gnocchi, with money under the plate for luck.' where id = '742f77df-09f7-552b-baff-76369529b3b3' and body_md = 'When the meat reaches the table, **se aplaude al asador**: *¡un aplauso para el asador!* **Se brinda** with everyone at the table. Leaving without saying goodbye to each person? Very **maleducado**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Se trae** algo. | You bring something. |
| **Se pone** la mesa. | The table gets set. |
| **Se brinda** con todos. | Everyone toasts together. |
| **Se aplaude** al asador. | Everyone applauds the grill master. |

**Se** + the *él* form: no subject, because it''s everybody. *Acá se come tarde* works the same way. As a guest you say **llevar**: **¿qué llevo?** — *what should I bring?* The host, already there, says **traer**: **¿quién trae el vino?**' where id = '79c02546-9daf-5168-b348-001f1c21de69' and body_md = '| **Se trae** algo. | You bring something. |
| **Se pone** la mesa. | The table gets set. |
| **Se brinda** con todos. | Everyone toasts together. |
| **Se aplaude** al asador. | Everyone applauds the grill master. |

**Se** + the *él* form: no subject, because it''s everybody. *Acá se come tarde* works the same way. On your way there, *bring* is **llevar**: **¿qué llevo?** — *what should I bring?*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me da asco la cucaracha**, **me dan asco las cucarachas** — the verb follows the thing. In the past: **¿te dio miedo?** — **no, me dio risa**.' where id = '605b9c23-3a8a-5a4d-bd8c-b8abb585d7f5' and body_md = '**Me da asco la cucaracha**, **me dan asco las cucarachas** — the verb follows the thing. In the story: **¿te dio miedo?** — **no, me dio risa**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'People say **la engañó** — *he cheated on her* — and in gossip even more often **le metió los cuernos**, literally *put the horns on*. **Engañar** is also plain *to trick, to fool*.', title_en = 'Los cuernos' where id = '026bd560-7714-5c78-9076-aba02a35b1d7' and body_md = 'In real gossip nobody says *lo engañó*: it is **le metió los cuernos** — *cheated on him/her*, literally *put the horns on*. **Engañar** is also plain *to trick, to fool*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| a fact — normal verb | a maybe — subjunctive |
| Aunque **llueve**, vamos. | Aunque **llueva**, vamos. |
| Aunque **cuesta**, sigo. | Aunque **cueste**, sigo. |
| Aunque **estoy** cansado, voy. | Aunque **esté** cansado, voy. |

Left: it *is* raining. Right: whether or not it rains. **Igual** at the end — *anyway* — often closes it.' where id = '63fad49e-94ca-595b-9a43-f0244cd997ff' and body_md = '| a fact — normal verb | a maybe — subjunctive |
| Aunque **llueve**, vamos. | Aunque **llueva**, vamos. |
| Aunque **cuesta**, sigo. | Aunque **cueste**, sigo. |
| Aunque no **querés**, tenés que ir. | Aunque no **quieras**, tenés que ir. |

Left: it *is* raining. Right: whether or not it rains. **Igual** at the end — *anyway* — often closes it.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Both start the second half: **sin embargo** — *however*, mostly in writing or formal talk — and the more spoken **así y todo** — *even so*: *hice dieta y **así y todo** engordé*.' where id = 'a86f3f75-92ae-5f8d-ad92-17fed3596c6b' and body_md = 'Both start the second half: **sin embargo** — *however*, mostly in writing or formal talk — and the more spoken **así y todo** — *even so*: *hice dieta; **así y todo**, engordé*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Hace un año que vivo acá** — *I''ve been living here for a year*: Spanish stays in the present. **Llevar** + time + *-ando / -iendo* says the same: **llevo un año viviendo acá**. Or just a place: **lleva un año acá**. With **sin**: **llevás tres días sin dormir**. To ask: **¿hace cuánto que vivís acá?** Day to day porteños say **hace… que**.', title_en = 'How long: llevar, hace… que' where id = '28e10253-628a-56be-99ee-ea69b41f5587' and body_md = '**Hace dos años que vivo acá** — *I''ve been living here for two years*. Where English says *have been …ing*, Spanish stays in the present. To ask: **¿hace cuánto que vivís acá?** or just **¿hace cuánto estás acá?**; **¿hace mucho que esperás?** — *have you been waiting long?* You will also hear **llevo dos años viviendo acá** — same meaning, but day to day porteños say **hace… que**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Seguir** + *-ando / -iendo* is *still doing* or *keep doing*: **sigo laburando ahí**, **¿seguís viviendo en San Telmo?** With a noun or adjective it is just *still*: **sigo cansado**, **¿seguís con fiebre?** **Seguir sin** + infinitive is *still not*: **¿seguís sin fumar?**', title_en = 'Sigo, seguís: still' where id = '75167017-65a6-5a49-9a02-adfb338b796b' and body_md = '| Llevo dos años **viviendo** acá. | I''ve been living here for two years. |
| Hace dos años que **vivo** acá. | (the same) |
| **Sigo** laburando ahí. | I still work there. |
| **Dejé de** fumar. | I quit smoking. |
| **Volvió a** llamar. | He called again. |
English *have been …ing* is the present in Spanish. With a past verb, **hace … que** means *ago*: *hace dos años que dejé de fumar* — *I quit two years ago*. **Llevar** + time + *-ando, -iendo* — or just a place: **lleva un año acá**. **Llevo / sigo sin** + infinitive is *haven''t … / still not*: *llevo seis meses sin fumar*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Lo que** is *what* when it means *the thing that*: **¿viste lo que pasó?**, **contame lo que pasó**. It is how every chisme starts: **no sabés lo que me contaron** — *you won''t believe what I heard*. A direct question keeps **qué**: *¿qué pasó?*', title_en = 'Lo que' where id = '457aa31e-c947-5f00-b748-3212e6826684' and body_md = '**No sabés lo que me contaron** — *you won''t believe what I heard* — is how every chisme starts. **Lo que** carries the whole story: **todo lo que pasó**, **lo que me dijo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¡No me digas!** and **¡callate!** both mean *no way!* — between friends *callate* isn''t rude. **¡Mirá vos!** is milder: *wow, really?* By the afternoon **todo el mundo** knows, thanks to the **chusma**: the person who loves gossip.', title_en = 'The reactions' where id = 'cba630fb-166d-5c75-b920-75b35d3ba605' and body_md = '**¡No me digas!** — *no way!*; **¡callate!** — between friends it isn''t rude, it means *you''re kidding!* And by the afternoon **todo el mundo** knows.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**De vez en cuando** is *every now and then*: **fumo de vez en cuando**. **Casi nunca** is *hardly ever*: **casi nunca manejo**. Both can be a whole answer: *¿Salís mucho? — De vez en cuando.* Your **rutina** is what you do every day.', title_en = 'How often?' where id = '559eee63-454f-5ebc-885f-9cdf45705eee' and body_md = 'The other persons of *soler*: **solemos juntarnos los viernes**, **los porteños suelen cenar tarde**. And *acabar de* for everyone: **acabamos de llegar**, **acaban de salir**. How often? **De vez en cuando**, or **casi nunca**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Mis viejos querían que estudiara** — the wish is in the past, so the second verb is too. **Por más que me cueste** — however hard it is. Something not sure or not real yet takes the subjunctive: *por más que llueva, vamos igual*. A fact takes the normal verb: *por más que ahorro, no me alcanza*.' where id = 'df9106c3-5bfc-57cc-b3da-428704d81c8e' and body_md = '**Mis viejos querían que estudiara** — the wish is in the past, so the second verb is too. **Por más que me cueste** — however hard it is: a maybe takes the subjunctive.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Hace un año que estudio** says the same as **llevo un año estudiando**. **Seguimos buscando** — *we''re still looking*; **volví a empezar** — *I started again*.' where id = '85402fa0-6355-51d2-b439-9abb4c3aa126' and body_md = '**Hace un año que estudio** says the same as **llevo un año estudiando**. **Seguimos buscando**, **volví a empezar**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Habla **como si supiera** todo. | He talks as if he knew everything. |
| **Como si fuera** fácil. | As if it were easy. |
| Me saludó **como si nada**. | He said hi as if nothing had happened. |
| ¡**Ni que fuera** tan difícil! | It''s not like it''s that hard! |

**Ni que…** is a complaint: you are saying the thing is NOT true. After **como si** and **ni que**, always the *-ra* form, whatever the time.' where id = 'd953b996-8823-5ff5-903a-37c8c6ca647c' and body_md = '| Habla **como si supiera** todo. | He talks as if he knew everything. |
| **Como si fuera** fácil. | As if it were easy. |
| Me saludó **como si nada**. | He said hi as if nothing had happened. |
| ¡**Ni que fuera** tan difícil! | It''s not like it''s that hard! |

After **como si** and **ni que**, always the *-ra* form, whatever the time.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Hacerse el** + a describing word is *to pretend, to act*: **me hice** el distraído — *I pretended not to notice*; **te hacés** el sordo — *you act like you can''t hear*; **se hace** el canchero — *he shows off, he acts all cool*. **No te hagas el gil** — *don''t play dumb*. A woman says **la**: *me hice **la** simpática*.', title_en = 'Hacerse el' where id = '3e245af1-6d97-5dae-8ef1-7ab6426eb575' and body_md = '| yo | **me hice** el distraído | I pretended not to notice |
| vos | **te hacés** el sordo | you act like you can''t hear |
| él, ella | **se hace** el canchero | he acts all cool |
| | como si no **pasara** nada | as if nothing were happening |
| | como si no me **viera** | as if he didn''t see me |

**No te hagas el gil** — *don''t play dumb*. A woman says **la**: *me hice **la** simpática*, *se hace **la** sorda*. After **como si** and **ni que**, always the *-ra* form: *¡ni que **fueras** mi viejo!* But **hace como que** takes a normal verb: *hace como que no le importa*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A **caradura** has no shame: never pays, asks for too much, lies and doesn''t feel bad about it. **¡Qué caradura!** — *you''ve got some nerve!* Between friends it''s often a joke.' where id = '8e0594ac-1009-51d2-b934-d91eaaa7f29c' and body_md = 'A **caradura** has no shame: never pays, asks for too much, lies with a straight face. **¡Qué caradura!** — *you''ve got some nerve!* Between friends it''s often a joke.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**El de** is also for owners and people. With a name it is *someone''s*: **el de Lucía** — *Lucía''s*; **las de Santi** — *Santi''s*. With people it is *the guy in, the people from*: **el de rojo** — *the guy in red*; **los de arriba** — *the people upstairs*.', title_en = 'El de Lucía, el de rojo' where id = 'd4f3c5be-cc6e-55ca-b459-5f8dcfb65deb' and body_md = 'Drop the noun, keep the article: **el de la vidriera** — *the one in the window*; **la de la izquierda** — *the one on the left*; **las de** allá. With a name it is *someone''s*: **el de Lucía** — *Lucía''s*. With people it is *the guy in, the people from*: **el de rojo** — *the guy in red*; **los de arriba** — *the people upstairs*. It matches what it stands for, like *el que*: **la que te probaste**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| yo, él, ella | **hubiera** | sabido, venido, ido |
| vos | **hubieras** | llamado, avisado, pensado |

For what didn''t happen, both halves: **Si hubiera sabido, te hubiera avisado.** *If I''d known, I''d have told you.* You will also hear **habría** in the second half: *te habría avisado*. Same meaning. Compare *si supiera* — if I knew (now).' where id = '058b9be3-593b-5386-8f79-4af1d6232d6f' and body_md = '| yo, él, ella | **hubiera** | sabido, venido, ido |
| vos | **hubieras** | llamado, avisado, pensado |

For what didn''t happen, both halves: **Si hubiera sabido, te hubiera avisado.** *If I''d known, I''d have told you.* Compare *si supiera* — if I knew (now).';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Hubiera** takes the participles *había* does: **sabido, venido, ido, llamado, dicho, hecho**. **Si hubieras venido** — *if you had come*. On its own it''s *would have* — *yo hubiera dicho que sí*, *I would have said yes* — or regret, *should have*: **ojalá hubiera estudiado** — *I wish I''d studied*; **¡me hubieras llamado!** — *you should have called me!*' where id = 'ff92a735-5164-5693-b16f-d442465b6dbe' and body_md = '**Hubiera** takes the participles *había* does: **sabido, venido, ido, llamado, dicho, hecho**. **Si hubieras venido** — *if you had come*. On its own it''s regret: **ojalá hubiera estudiado** — *I wish I''d studied*; **¡me hubieras llamado!** — *you should have called me!*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To give your view, porteños say **para mí** or **me parece que**: *para mí conviene esperar*; *me parece que es caro*. **¿Qué opinás?** is the natural question; **opino que…** as an answer sounds stiff. **No me convence** — *I''m not sure about it* — works like *gustar*.' where id = 'd0bec188-cd5e-5f50-8ea4-f2be488d6a42' and body_md = 'To give your view, porteños say **para mí** or **me parece que**: *para mí conviene esperar*; *me parece que es caro*. **¿Qué opinás?** is the natural question; **opino que…** as an answer sounds stiff.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Por lo menos** — *at least* — finds the good side: *pagan poco, pero **por lo menos** queda cerca*. **La verdad** — *honestly* — says what you really think: ***la verdad**, no me conviene*. **Conviene** works like *gustar*: **me conviene** — *it''s better for me*; **te conviene llevar paraguas** — *it''s a good idea to take an umbrella*.' where id = '65ee37e5-32e4-5795-acaa-8f3a37e6f50c' and body_md = '**Por lo menos** — *at least* — finds the good side: *pagan poco, pero **por lo menos** queda cerca*. **La verdad** — *honestly* — says what you really think: ***la verdad**, no me conviene*. **Conviene** works like *gustar*: **me conviene** — *it''s better for me*; **te conviene llevar paraguas** — *you''d better take an umbrella*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'After **como si** and **ni que**, always the *-ra* form: **como si no pasara nada** — *as if nothing were happening*; **como si no me viera** — *as if he didn''t see me*; **¡ni que fueras mi viejo!** — *it''s not like you''re my dad!* But **hace como que** takes a normal verb: *hace como que no le importa* — *he acts like he doesn''t care*.', title_en = 'Como si no pasara nada' where id = 'c22a6a2e-e9a5-541b-934c-80c0b380fc22' and body_md = '**Importar** works like *gustar*: **mi familia me importa** — *my family matters to me*; **¿a quién le importa?** — *who cares?*; **no importa** — *it doesn''t matter*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'An argument in Buenos Aires is a sport, not a fight: **discutimos** a lot and stay friends. To reject a point, say **¡nada que ver!** — *not at all!* (it can also mean *nothing alike* or *nothing to do with it*). If the other person won''t listen: **no seas cabeza dura** — *don''t be so stubborn*.', title_en = '¡Nada que ver!' where id = '1257cd1c-a853-5a83-8483-1b544c971a7b' and body_md = '**¡Nada que ver!** — *that''s got nothing to do with it!* — is how porteños throw out a point. **En eso** tenés razón concedes just the one. **No seas cabeza dura** — *don''t be so stubborn*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**A ver** — *let''s see* — slows an argument down. **Pensándolo bien** — *on second thought* — is how you change sides: *pensándolo bien, me convenciste* — *on second thought, you convinced me*. To heat it up again: **sos un exagerado** — *you''re being dramatic*.', title_en = 'A ver, pensándolo bien' where id = '3a35b239-66d5-5069-9a26-1a37d49b5555' and body_md = '**A ver** — *let''s see* — slows an argument down; **pensándolo bien** — *thinking about it* — is how you change sides without losing face. **Sos un exagerado** speeds it back up.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The hardest words in any argument: **me equivoqué** — *I was wrong*. To a friend: **te equivocás** — *you''re wrong*. To admit it: **reconozco que** tenés razón — *I admit you''re right* — or just **te doy la razón** — *you''re right*. **En eso** te doy la razón — *you''re right about that* — admits only one point.' where id = 'b93ba3b3-6a29-5ed3-a84e-307bfd07bb7b' and body_md = 'The hardest words in any argument: **me equivoqué** — *I was wrong*. To a friend: **te equivocás** — *you''re wrong*. Giving ground: **reconozco que** tenés razón, or just **te doy la razón**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To rent in Buenos Aires you need a **garantía** — *a guarantor*, usually a relative who owns property: *mi papá me sale de garantía* — *my dad is my guarantor*. No garantía? Foreigners often pay a **seguro de caución** — *rent guarantee insurance* — or take an **alquiler temporario amoblado** — *a furnished short-term rental*.', title_en = 'La garantía' where id = 'b52a18e2-e627-5862-85be-cadba86191d4' and body_md = 'Renting in Buenos Aires means the **inmobiliaria** asks for a **garantía** — a relative''s property as a guarantee — and a **contrato**. Foreigners usually take an **alquiler temporario** — *a short-term rental*, **amoblado** — or pay a **seguro de caución** instead of the garantía, plus a **depósito**. Ask about the **expensas** (the monthly building fees) and how many **ambientes** it has: *un dos ambientes* is one bedroom and a living room. Some **dueños** don''t take **mascotas**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Me **pone nervioso** que llegue tarde. | It annoys me when he''s late. |
| Me **enoja** que me **mienta**. | It makes me angry that he lies to me. |
| Me **alegra** que vengas. | I''m glad you''re coming. |
| Me da bronca que **cancele**. | It makes me mad that he cancels. |

Feeling first, then **que** + subjunctive. **Nervioso** here is often *annoyed* or *tense*, not only *nervous*. If it''s you doing it, no *que*: *me enoja **llegar** tarde*.' where id = '71b73b1e-ae85-5fc6-9381-abc5a40d2806' and body_md = '| Me **pone nervioso** que llegue tarde. | It makes me nervous that he''s late. |
| Me **enoja** que me **mienta**. | It makes me angry that he lies to me. |
| Me **alegra** que vengas. | I''m glad you''re coming. |
| Me da bronca que **cancele**. | It makes me mad that he cancels. |

Feeling first, then **que** + subjunctive. If it''s you doing it, no *que*: *me enoja **llegar** tarde*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| yo, él, ella | **debería** |
| vos | **deberías** |
| nosotros | **deberíamos** |
| ellos, ustedes | **deberían** |

All take an infinitive: *deberíamos juntarnos*. *En esa empresa **deberían** pagar mejor* — *that company should pay better*.' where id = 'db21a125-f08f-5134-aec7-53e13720f369' and body_md = '| yo, él, ella | **debería** |
| vos | **deberías** |
| nosotros | **deberíamos** |
| ellos, ustedes | **deberían** |

All take an infinitive: *deberíamos juntarnos*. **Estaría bueno que** + subjunctive when there''s a person: *estaría bueno que te tomes unos días*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When you say who should do it, use **que** + subjunctive: **estaría bueno que te tomes unos días** — *it''d be good if you took a few days off*. For people in general, the infinitive: *estaría bueno **descansar***. And the push: **¡animate!** — *go for it!*', title_en = 'Estaría bueno que…' where id = 'ba67d83b-3d37-5a5b-a746-77aba5677455' and body_md = 'With a person after it, **que** + subjunctive: **estaría bueno que te tomes unos días**. Without one, the infinitive: *estaría bueno **descansar***. And the push: **¡animate!** — *go for it!*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me prometiste que ibas a venir** — *you promised me you''d come* (more careful: *que vendrías*). And the classic ending: **al final no vino** — *in the end he didn''t come*. If he did, he **cumplió** — *kept his word*: *prometió llamar y cumplió*.' where id = '3960dc2b-904b-5a87-9ca3-02e2ae3c3968' and body_md = '**Me prometiste que ibas a venir** — *you promised me you''d come* (more careful: *que vendrías*). And the classic ending: **al final no vino**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To stress a promise, porteños say **me aseguró que…** — *he assured me* — or **me juró que…** — *he swore*. Then **me puso una excusa** — *he gave me an excuse* — and you learn not to **confiar en** (*trust*) the **mentiroso** (*liar*).' where id = '5aaa801b-ae20-5109-886b-c9cff7a1d334' and body_md = 'To stress a promise, porteños say **me aseguró que…** — *he assured me* — or **me juró que…** — *he swore*. Then comes the **excusa** (*excuse*), and you learn not to **confiar en** (*trust*) the **mentiroso** (*liar*).';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When someone lends you something, the conditions come fast: *te lo presto, con tal de que lo **cuides**, no lo **choques** y me lo **devuelvas entero***. The warning at the end is **si no** — *otherwise*: *si no, no te presto nada más*.', title_en = 'Que no lo choques' where id = '7d0442f0-ca98-54db-82a0-1b2b8177f436' and body_md = 'The *vos* subjunctive is the one you hear on the way out the door: *te lo presto, siempre y cuando no lo **choques**, lo **cuides** y me lo **devuelvas entero***. The last word: **si no**, *no te presto nada más*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Ando buscando** laburo. | I''ve been looking for work. |
| **Voy conociendo** gente. | I''m getting to know people. |
| **Estamos por** arrancar. | We''re about to start. |
| Estoy **a punto de** terminar. | I''m just about to finish. |

**Ando** + *-ando* is these days, on and off, not this very second; **voy** + *-ando* happens bit by bit.' where id = 'ec66006c-2d54-5e6c-9c71-4c5cc4a097d1' and body_md = '| **Ando buscando** laburo. | I''m looking around for work. |
| **Voy conociendo** gente. | I''m getting to know people. |
| **Estamos por** arrancar. | We''re about to start. |
| Estoy **a punto de** terminar. | I''m just about to finish. |

**Ando** + *-ando* is these days, on and off, not this very second; **voy** + *-ando* happens bit by bit.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estamos por arrancar** — *we''re about to start*. **A punto de** is a little stronger — *any second now*: **estoy a punto de terminar**.' where id = '5bbac630-a58e-519b-b308-312edbba56a6' and body_md = '**Estamos por arrancar** — *we''re about to start*. **A punto de** means the same, only even sooner: **estoy a punto de terminar**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Ando buscando laburo** — *I''ve been looking for work*: **ando** + *-ando* is these days. **Estamos por arrancar** — *we''re about to start*. **Le cae bien a todo el mundo** — *everybody likes him*; **a ese no lo aguanto** — *I can''t stand that guy*.' where id = '09c42605-395e-554f-8c40-6ffd14be9063' and body_md = '**Ando buscando laburo**, **estamos por arrancar**. **Le cae bien a todo el mundo**; **a ese no lo aguanto**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The small talk of bills: **aumentaron la luz y el gas** — *electricity and gas went up*; **el boleto subió** — *the fare went up*; **no llego a fin de mes** — *I can''t make ends meet*: the money runs out before the month does.', title_en = 'Aumentaron la luz' where id = '97c5fbb3-3689-5121-8618-b57a9378bab5' and body_md = '**Aumentaron la luz y el gas**, **el boleto subió**, **no llego a fin de mes** — the small talk of bills.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Ni a palos** — *no way, not a chance*. And for a shrug: **dale que va** — *good enough, let''s go*. When something''s awful: **está de terror**; when it''s perfect: **impecable**.' where id = 'e2b47401-0cfc-5d9f-9194-4ecbb72de555' and body_md = '**Ni a palos** — *no way, not a chance*. And for a shrug: **dale que va** — *good enough, let''s go*. When something''s awful: **está de terror**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Said slowly, **sí, claro** means *yeah, right*. **¡Qué novedad!** — *what a surprise* — is for the bondi that''s late again; **¡lo que faltaba!** — *that''s all we needed* — for the rain that starts on top of it. The everyday ones: **qué raro**, said flat — *¿llegó tarde? Qué raro.* — and **mirá vos** — *well, look at that*. The **tono** — *tone* — does the work.' where id = 'bb2b8f8c-6dae-5623-9c59-9a450c30bb65' and body_md = 'Said slowly, **sí, claro** means *yeah, right*. **¡Qué novedad!** — *what a surprise* — is for the bondi that''s late again; **¡lo que faltaba!** — *that''s all we needed* — for the rain that starts on top of it. The everyday ones: **qué raro**, said flat — *¿llegó tarde? Qué raro.* — and **mirá vos** — *well, look at that*. The tone does the work.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estoy al horno** — *I''m in big trouble*. **Qué bajón** — *what a shame*. **Al pedo** — *for nothing, doing nothing*: **fui al pedo**, **estoy al pedo**. And the flat *no way*: **ni en pedo**. The other *pedo* phrases: **estar en pedo** — *to be drunk*; **de pedo** — *by pure luck*: *llegué de pedo*. Among friends only.' where id = '1db93231-c31c-5630-a9d7-a5c19c863dd1' and body_md = '**Estoy al horno** — *I''m in trouble, I''m toast*. **Qué bajón** — *what a downer*. **Al pedo** — *for nothing, doing nothing*: **fui al pedo**, **estoy al pedo**. And the flat *no way*: **ni en pedo**. The other *pedo* phrases: **estar en pedo** — *to be drunk*; **de pedo** — *by pure luck*: *llegué de pedo*; **a los pedos** — *very fast*. Among friends only.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'People get labels: a **rata** never pays; a **careta** is fake or uptight (or someone who doesn''t drink or party); **grasa** is tacky (a snobbish word: fine as a joke about a shirt, rude about a person). **Estar manija** is to be very excited about something: **estoy manija con el recital**. The **cana** is the police. A friend who backs you **te hace la gamba**; one who talks nonsense **manda fruta**.' where id = '361c790d-a0af-59b6-8330-323cd924f6a0' and body_md = 'People get labels: a **rata** never pays; a **careta** is fake or uptight (or someone who doesn''t drink or party); **grasa** is tacky. **Estar manija** is to be very excited about something: **estoy manija con el recital**. The **cana** is the police. A friend who backs you **te hace la gamba**; one who talks nonsense **manda fruta**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'If someone **se calentó** — *got mad* — or **se ofendió** — *took offense* — the joke went too far. **Se picó**: a game or an argument got heated. An **apodo** (*nickname*) like **el Gordo** or **el Pelado** is friendly among friends; never use one with someone you just met.', title_en = 'Se calentó, apodos' where id = 'a3dfd806-54f5-516a-a10e-12f1e87569d8' and body_md = 'The joke only works if nobody takes it badly: **se calentó** — *he got mad* — and **se ofendió** — *he took offense* — are the worst things to say about someone at an asado. **Se picó** is what porteños say when a match or an argument got heated: *se picó el partido*. Everybody has an **apodo** — *a nickname*: **el Flaco**, **el Gordo**, **el Negro**, **el Pelado**, **el Colo** (the redhead). They are friendly, not insults: *le dicen el Flaco*. A **broma** — *a prank* — is a sign of affection too. **No te hagas el vivo**, though: **te hacés el vivo** is *you''re trying to be clever, to take advantage of someone*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Insistió en que fuera** — *she insisted I go*. **Me sugirió que la llamara** — *he suggested I call her*. As in *me pidió que trajera*, the verb after **que** is in the past subjunctive (*fuera, llamara*).' where id = '31e9d7c0-8868-567b-a709-775f9c735a92' and body_md = '**Insistió en que fuera** — *she insisted I go*. **Me sugirió que la llamara** — *he suggested I call her*. Same pattern: the verb after **que** in the past subjunctive.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A yes/no question told later uses **si** (*whether*): *¿Venís?* → **me preguntó si venía**; *¿Abre hoy?* → **no sé si abre hoy**. The verb is normal, no subjunctive. Told in the past, it usually moves back: *venís* → *venía*.' where id = 'e4034940-c3b8-5953-be43-6edfb0a0421a' and body_md = '| «¿Venís?» | Me preguntó **si** venía. |
| «¿Abre hoy?» | No sé **si** abre hoy. |
| | **A ver si** nos juntamos. |

A yes-or-no question told later hangs on **si**, with the normal verb.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Lo dije en joda** — *I said it as a joke*. **Tomar el pelo** is the same game as cargar: **¿me estás tomando el pelo?** — *are you joking with me?* **¿Me estás jodiendo?** is very casual: friends only. A **broma** is a prank, or something not said seriously.', title_en = 'En joda' where id = 'e7590664-dc43-56d6-aa5e-259e9a000d5b' and body_md = '**Lo dije en joda** — *I was joking*. A **chiste** is a joke you tell; if it lands, it''s **gracioso**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When someone believes your joke: **¡caíste!** — *got you!* — and **qué inocente** — *you''re so easy to trick*. If they complain too much: **estás exagerando** — *you''re overdoing it*. **Te hacés el vivo** — *you''re trying to be clever* — is for someone who tries to take advantage of others.', title_en = '¡Caíste!' where id = '6044efe3-ab79-5a6e-bf86-377632411a37' and body_md = '**Estar** + the **-ando / -iendo** form is how you catch a joke in progress: **me estás tomando el pelo** — *you''re joking with me*; **¿me estás jodiendo?** — *you''re kidding me*; **estás exagerando**. And when you believed it: **¡caíste!** — *got you!* — **qué inocente**. **Jodiendo** and **en joda** are very casual: fine with friends, not with a boss. Safer: **¿me estás cargando?**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'With older neighbours like **don José** and **doña Marta** you still say vos, but warmly: **cómo no** — *of course*; **faltaba más** — *of course, don''t mention it*; **dejá, te doy una mano** — *leave it, I''ll give you a hand*.', title_en = 'Cómo no, faltaba más' where id = 'e05a6f2c-db31-58b3-91ea-a33abfd335c9' and body_md = 'With **don José** and **doña Rosa**: **te doy una mano**, **dejá**, **cómo no**, **faltaba más** — vos, said warmly.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Sobre la hora** — *right at the deadline, at the very last minute* — is how most porteño projects get done. First a **borrador** — *a draft* — then you **corregir** it, and only then the **informe** or the **presentación**. **¿Avanzaron?** — *any progress?*' where id = '5b512731-476b-5b5f-8876-82ce3e6b19a4' and body_md = '**Sobre la hora** — *right at the deadline, with seconds to spare* — is how most porteño projects get done. First a **borrador** — *a draft* — then you **corregir** it, and only then the **informe** or the **presentación**. **¿Avanzaron?** — *any progress?*';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Me merezco** un aumento. | I deserve a raise. |
| **Me lo merezco.** | I deserve it. |
| **Te lo merecés.** | You deserve it. |
**Merecerse** usually comes with its pronoun in speech: the bare *merezco* is correct but more formal. **Valorar** is *to value*: *en mi laburo no me valoran* — *at my job they don''t value me*.' where id = '5f8b9622-8605-59be-9a2c-df64d8920c28' and body_md = '| **Me merezco** un aumento. | I deserve a raise. |
| **Me lo merezco.** | I deserve it. |
| **Te lo merecés.** | You deserve it. |
**Merecerse** usually comes with its pronoun in speech: the bare *merezco* is correct but more formal. And a boss who **valora** your work — *values* it — says so with the sueldo.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me la banco** — *I can handle it*; **se la bancó** — *she put up with it*. To say you can''t stand something, drop the **la** and name it: *no me banco este frío* — *I can''t stand this cold*; *no me banco a mi jefe* — *I can''t stand my boss*.', title_en = 'Bancar, bancársela' where id = '24f0169c-f457-5099-922f-4a497b84e8df' and body_md = 'A little **la** that points at nothing turns a verb into an idiom: **se la cree** — *he''s full of himself*; **me la banco** — *I can handle it*; **la tenés clara** — *you know your stuff*. With **las**: **me las arreglo** — *I get by*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Two fixed phrases to learn whole: **a las apuradas** — *in a rush* — and **a la larga** — *in the long run*. Here *las* and *la* are just *the*, not the idiom''s *la*: *salí a las apuradas y me olvidé las llaves*.', title_en = 'A las apuradas, a la larga' where id = '64ddc740-cba3-541e-b01d-38bbf52e9139' and body_md = 'The *la* stays put while the person changes: **me la banco**, **te la bancás**, **nos la bancamos**; **me las arreglo**, **te las arreglás**, **se las arregla**. Two more with the *la* inside: **a las apuradas** — *in a rush* — and **a la larga** — *in the long run*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| yo | vos | él, ella |
| **me la banco** | **te la bancás** | **se la bancó** |
| **me las arreglo** | **te las arreglás** | **se las arregla** |

Some verbs carry *me, te, se* plus the *la*; others just the *la*: **la pifié**, **la pifiaste**; **la rompiste**, **la rompe**. The *la* never changes.', title_en = 'The la stays, the person changes' where id = 'd2483fff-67ae-5148-81e8-91d76e90d333' and body_md = '| yo | vos | él, ella |
| **me la banco** | **te la bancás** | **se la bancó** |
| **me las arreglo** | **te las arreglás** | **se las arregla** |
| **me la jugué** | **la pifiaste** | **se la agarró** |
| **me las tomo** | **la rompiste** | **la rompe** |

Some verbs carry *me, te, se* plus the *la*; others (*pifiarla, romperla*) just the *la*. The *la* never changes.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Te reenvío el archivo** — *I''m forwarding you the file*; **cualquier duda, avisame** — *any questions, let me know*. And the story: **de golpe** — *all of a sudden*; **para colmo** — *to top it all off*; **por lo visto** — *apparently*.' where id = '915c227f-3a59-5eb0-8e94-a3be77cd232d' and body_md = '**Te reenvío el archivo**, **cualquier duda, avisame**. And the story: **de golpe**, **para colmo**, **por lo visto**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Dejé de fumar**, **volvió a correr**, **solemos cenar tarde**.' where id = '68ee52b6-ffc4-510b-819b-25355d531ada' and body_md = '**Dejé de fumar**, **volvió a correr**, **solemos cenar tarde**, **acabamos de llegar**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Y bueno** is the porteño shrug — *oh well, what can you do*: **y bueno, así es**. **Ah, me olvidaba** — *oh, I almost forgot* — adds the best part at the end. A story can be **larga** — *long* — or **corta** — *short*.' where id = 'c94d2e69-9d48-539a-a1af-33cdcb771363' and body_md = '**Y bueno** is the porteño shrug — *oh well, what can you do*: **y bueno, así es**. **Ah, me olvidaba** — *oh, I forgot to say* — adds the best part at the end. A story can be **larga** — *long* — or **corta** — *short*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The morning after, the question is what still runs: **el subte funciona con normalidad**, or **suspendieron el servicio**. When the strike itself ends, the phrase is **levantaron el paro** or **se levantó el paro**. **Suspender** is for classes, an exam, a march or a service.', title_en = 'Levantaron el paro' where id = 'ee61df72-edc1-551c-8a85-ffd52d0c70ad' and body_md = 'The morning after, the question is what still runs: **el subte funciona con normalidad**, or **suspendieron el servicio**. When the strike itself is called off, the fixed phrase is **levantaron el paro** / **se levantó el paro**; *suspender* is for classes, an exam, a march or a service. **Hubo un apagón** — *there was a blackout* — and the traffic lights are out: **embotellamiento**, **desvíos**, and half the city goes **a pie**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| El puente **fue construido** hace un siglo. | was built |
| La estación **fue inaugurada** ayer. | was opened |
| Los ladrones **fueron detenidos**. | were arrested |

**Fue** + participle, and the participle agrees like an adjective. **Detenidos** is also a noun: *hay dos detenidos* — *two people were arrested*.' where id = 'de7cd7bc-7f0d-588c-bc69-c90f2dc4f004' and body_md = '| El puente **fue construido** hace un siglo. | was built |
| La estación **fue inaugurada** ayer. | was opened |
| Los chorros **fueron detenidos**. | were arrested |

**Fue** + participle, and the participle agrees like an adjective. In conversation: *construyeron el puente*. **Detenidos** is also a noun: *hay dos detenidos* — *two people were arrested*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The news says **fue construido**; in conversation porteños turn it around: *construyeron el puente*, *los detuvieron*. Or they use **se**: **el puente se inauguró ayer**, **se construyó hace un siglo**. For the future the news says **será inaugurada** — *will be opened*; people say *la van a inaugurar*.', title_en = 'In conversation' where id = '5f88a88d-8066-58cb-99c8-edeb9d5d9112' and body_md = 'The news likes the passive: **fue** + participle, and the participle agrees like an adjective: **el puente fue construido**, **la estación fue inaugurada**; more than one: **fueron detenidos** — *they were arrested*. In conversation porteños turn it around: *construyeron el puente*, *los detuvieron*. For the future the news says **será inaugurada** — *will be opened*; people say *la van a inaugurar*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Aparentemente** is the neutral *apparently*: **aparentemente, mañana hay paro**. **Se ve que** is what you conclude from what you see: **se ve que llovió** — *it must have rained*; **se ve que está cerrado**.', title_en = 'Aparentemente, se ve que' where id = '6d88948a-49cd-507f-b390-3b282380d755' and body_md = '**Según** takes people as well as papers: **según él**, **según ellos**, **según la fuente**. **Aparentemente** is the neutral *apparently*; **se ve que** is what you conclude from what you see: **se ve que llovió** — *it must have rained*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'In Argentina voting is **obligatorio** from 18 to 70. **¿A quién votaste?** is a real question, though many people don''t answer it. **Votar a** someone: *voté a otro candidato*. **Votar por** works too: *¿por quién votás?* **Votar en blanco** is to cast a blank vote.', title_en = 'Votar' where id = '67c1e923-9983-5e50-a6ce-52ff85a6eb09' and body_md = 'In Argentina voting is **obligatorio** from 18 to 70 (optional at 16–17 and after 70). **¿A quién votaste?** is a real question, though many answer **eso no se pregunta**. **Votar a** someone: *voté a la misma candidata*. **Votar por** works too: *¿por quién votás?* **Votar en blanco** is to cast a blank vote. And from the night before there is **veda**: no campaigning, and shops and bars can''t sell alcohol.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Election day is a Sunday, and everyone asks **¿dónde votás?** — usually at a school near home: **votamos en la misma escuela**. Before it there is **veda**: campaigning stops 48 hours before the vote, and from the night before nobody can sell alcohol.', title_en = '¿Dónde votás?' where id = '2a3a2462-0e4e-58df-9bc1-fcf6e909f66e' and body_md = 'Election day is a Sunday, and everyone asks **¿dónde votás?** You check the **padrón** — *the voter roll* — for your school and your **mesa** — *your voting table*. **Votamos** in the school around the corner; **mi abuela votó a las ocho**, first in line.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Las elecciones** — *the elections* — decide the **gobierno** and the **presidente**. Before them, the **debate** on TV; after, the **resultados**. If nobody wins outright there''s a **balotaje** — *a runoff*. The course stays out of who won: the words, not the opinions.', title_en = 'Las elecciones' where id = 'eac6d092-ac6a-51cb-ad45-36a8a79f1e96' and body_md = '**Las elecciones** — *the elections* — decide the **gobierno** and the **presidente**. The course stays out of it: the words, not the opinions.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Según** — *according to* — takes papers and people: **según el diario**, **según mi mamá**, **según Nico**. **Supuestamente** and **al parecer** keep a distance from what you pass on. **Al parecer** sounds like the news; in chat people say *parece que*.', title_en = 'Según' where id = '5c404af7-97bb-5016-95f3-4dbb7f00df17' and body_md = '**Según** — *according to*: **según el diario**, **según mi vieja**. **Al parecer** and **supuestamente** keep a distance from what you''re passing on. **Al parecer** sounds like the news; in chat people say **por lo visto** or **parece que**: *por lo visto, Sofi tiene novio nuevo*; *parece que no viene*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A **rumor** is only that until someone **confirma** it, or denies it: **el gobierno desmintió el rumor**. Before **compartirlo**, ask **¿cuál es la fuente?** A **cadena** — *a chain message* — with no source is probably **verso** — *made up*.', title_en = '¿Rumor o verso?' where id = '3ff85211-a894-5d45-b66e-973838dc3d86' and body_md = 'A story is **confirmado** or it''s **desmentido**: **el gremio desmintió el rumor**, **lo desmintieron en el noticiero**. Before you forward it, ask **¿cuál es la fuente?** — the **titular** says one thing, the **versión oficial** another.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Fue clausurado** is the event — *it got closed down*; **está clausurado** is the result — *it is closed now*. The ending agrees with the thing: **el boliche fue clausurado**, **la obra fue clausurada**, **la cancha está clausurada**.', title_en = 'Fue clausurado, está clausurado' where id = '22681126-952e-59e5-97e2-12d780e48738' and body_md = 'Both parts agree with what it''s about — **fue**/**fueron** for one or many, and the ending **-o/-a/-os/-as**: **el boliche fue clausurado**, **la obra fue clausurada**, **los vecinos fueron rescatados**, **las vecinas fueron rescatadas**. Whoever did it comes after **por**: *por los bomberos*. **Fue clausurado** is the event — *it got closed down*; **está clausurado** is the result — *it is closed now*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| one | more than one |
| El boliche **fue clausurado**. | Los vecinos **fueron rescatados**. |
| La obra **fue clausurada**. | Las vecinas **fueron rescatadas**. |
| La ley **fue aprobada**. | Los heridos **fueron trasladados**. |

Who did it comes after **por**: *por los bomberos*. ' where id = '501e88f5-eb36-539f-8d0e-30b521ee54d7' and body_md = '| one | more than one |
| El boliche **fue clausurado**. | Los vecinos **fueron rescatados**. |
| La obra **fue clausurada**. | Las vecinas **fueron rescatadas**. |
| La ley **fue aprobada**. | Los heridos **fueron trasladados**. |

Who did it comes after **por**: *por los bomberos*. The news opens with **hubo**: *hubo un incendio*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Put **lo** before an adjective to say *the … thing*: **lo lindo** — *the nice thing*, **lo feo** — *the bad part*, **lo único** — *the only thing*. Add **de** to say of what: **lo peor de Buenos Aires es el tránsito**. **Lo** never changes: **lo feo son los precios**.', title_en = 'Lo + adjective' where id = '7ae297c7-20ed-5a6a-976d-9efc0c4c19d4' and body_md = '| **Lo lindo** es que siempre hay algo. | The nice thing is there''s always something. |
| **Lo feo** es el tránsito. | The ugly part is the traffic. |
| **Lo difícil** fue el idioma. | The hard part was the language. |
| **Lo único** que extraño es el mar. | The only thing I miss is the sea. |
| **Lo más** lindo es la plaza del barrio. | The nicest thing is the local square. |

**Lo** + adjective makes *the … thing*, and **lo** never becomes la, los or las. With a plural noun, the verb is plural: **lo feo son los precios**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To say the good and the bad together: **Buenos Aires tiene sus cosas** — *it has its issues* — like the **inseguridad** (*crime*) and the **costo de vida** (*cost of living*). But **a la vez** — *at the same time* — **no hay nada como Buenos Aires**: *there''s nothing like it*.', title_en = 'Tiene sus cosas' where id = 'a75b10b9-a779-55fa-ae70-312528aa56c8' and body_md = '**Lo más** + adjective is *the most … thing*: **lo más lindo del barrio es la plaza**. Weighing it up, porteños say the city **tiene sus cosas** — *has its issues*: the **inseguridad**, the **costo de vida** — but the **calidad de vida**, **a la vez**, is hard to beat.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'After **no es que** any verb goes into the subjunctive, and you already know the forms: **sea**, **esté**, **haya**, **tenga**. *No es que sea caro, es que no tengo plata* — *it''s not that it''s expensive, I just have no money*. *No es que esté cansado, es que laburo temprano.*', title_en = 'No es que sea' where id = 'e4442fba-2d7d-515f-bf95-5182892f4c7e' and body_md = 'A reason you deny takes the subjunctive: **no es que no quiera** — *it''s not that I don''t want to*. The real reason follows with **es que** and the normal verb: **es que no puedo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Nobody wants to **quedar mal** — *look rude*. So you thank them for the **invitación**, blame a **compromiso** — *other plans* — and leave the door open: **la próxima voy**, **otro día**. And if they push: **no insistas, che**. **Rechazar** needs something after it — *rechacé dos invitaciones* — and sounds formal; day to day people say **decir que no**: *me cuesta decir que no*.' where id = 'cc5e231d-b0ac-5861-be50-d1802854aad9' and body_md = 'Nobody wants to **quedar mal** — *look rude*. So you thank them for the **invitación**, blame a **compromiso** — *a prior commitment* — and leave the door open: **la próxima voy**, **otro día**. And if they push: **no insistas, che**. **Rechazar** needs something after it — *rechacé dos invitaciones* — and sounds formal; day to day people say **decir que no**: *me cuesta decir que no*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'After **no es que**, every verb goes subjunctive: **no es que no me interese** — *it''s not that I''m not interested*; **no es que no me importe** — *it''s not that I don''t care*; **no es que me caiga mal** — *it''s not that I don''t like him*; **no es que no queramos / podamos** — *it''s not that we don''t want to / can''t*. The real reason follows with **es que** + a normal verb: *es que no llego* — *I just can''t make it*.', title_en = 'No es que…, es que…' where id = '2f545600-080d-50bc-8cb8-ceb5c9b0db7e' and body_md = '| **No es que** no me **interese**, | It''s not that I''m not interested, |
| **No es que** no me **importe**, | It''s not that I don''t care, |
| **No es que** me **caiga** mal, | It''s not that I don''t like him, |
| **No es que** no **queramos**, | It''s not that we don''t want to, |
| **es que** tengo un compromiso. | it''s just that I have plans. |
The denied reason is subjunctive in every person — **no es que no podamos** too; the real one after **es que** is not. Don''t push: **no insistas**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Hubiera** + participle also works alone as *would have*: **nunca lo hubiera vendido** — *I''d never have sold it*; **¿lo hubieras vendido?** — *would you have sold it?* And **ojalá hubiera** + participle is *I wish I had*: **ojalá hubiera ahorrado más**.', title_en = 'Would have, I wish I had' where id = 'fdea7949-7c65-5ef1-92db-aafc9dc74362' and body_md = 'With *we*: **si hubiéramos salido antes, ya estaríamos ahí**. The participles: **ahorrado, comprado, vendido, aceptado**. **Hubiera** + participle also works alone as *would have*: **nunca lo hubiera vendido** — *I''d never have sold it*; **yo que vos, no lo hubiera vendido**. With *vos* it is **hubieras**: **¿lo hubieras vendido?** And **ojalá hubiera** + participle = *I wish I had*: **ojalá hubiera ahorrado más**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Hubiera** changes with the person: **hubiera** (I, he, she), **hubieras** (vos), **hubiéramos** (we), **hubieran** (they, you all). *Si hubieras estudiado medicina, ahora serías médico. Si hubiéramos ahorrado, ahora estaríamos en Bariloche. Si hubieran construido el puente, no habría tanto tránsito.*', title_en = 'Hubiera, hubieras, hubiéramos, hubieran' where id = 'e7e97709-b1ce-5787-93fb-a7735a2015ce' and body_md = 'The mixed conditional with *you*: **si hubieras estudiado medicina, ahora serías médico**; **si me hubieras hecho caso, no estarías así**. With *we*: **si hubiéramos ahorrado, ahora tendríamos para las vacaciones**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me arrepiento** — *I regret it*; **me arrepentí** — *I regretted it, I changed my mind*. With what you did or didn''t do, **de (no) haber** + participle: **me arrepiento de no haber ido** — *I regret not going*; *no me arrepiento de haber venido*. An **oportunidad** is a chance; **aprovechar** is to make the most of it: *no aproveché la oportunidad*.' where id = '8a29fec5-b96f-5019-8de7-6e3c598a5302' and body_md = '**Me arrepiento** — *I regret it*; **me arrepentí** — *I regretted it, I changed my mind*. With what you did or didn''t do, **de (no) haber** + participle: **me arrepiento de no haber ido** — *I regret not going*; *no me arrepiento de haber venido*. A missed chance is a **oportunidad** you didn''t **aprovechar**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Metí la pata** — *I messed up, I said or did the wrong thing*. More porteño: **me mandé una macana**. A **macana** is a silly mistake; an **error** is any mistake. And when something goes wrong for someone: **¡qué macana!** — *what a shame!*', title_en = 'Metí la pata' where id = '54279426-a9ab-597a-90c9-2ebc30ce6253' and body_md = 'With *vos*: **¿te arrepentís?**; with *him*: **se arrepintió**. **Dejé pasar la oportunidad** — *I let the chance go*. **Te lo perdiste** — *you missed out*. **Metí la pata** — *I made a mistake, I said or did the wrong thing* — or, more porteño, **me mandé una macana**. **¡Qué macana!** — *what a shame*. **Lamentablemente**, you can''t **volver atrás** — so you drop it with **ya fue**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A chance you let go: **dejé pasar la oportunidad** — *I let the chance go*. To someone who didn''t come: **te lo perdiste** — *you missed out*. **Lamentablemente** — *unfortunately* — you can''t **volver atrás** — *go back* — so you drop it with **ya fue**.', title_en = 'Te lo perdiste' where id = '1d43e9b9-80e9-5f3c-b2cb-a7c32890b5fc' and body_md = 'On its own, **hubieras** + participle is a reproach — *you should have*: **¡hubieras avisado!** — *you should have told me!* As a question it is *would you have…?*: **¿hubieras ido?** And for *we shouldn''t have*, add **no**: **no tendríamos que haber venido**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Another life: **si hubieras estudiado, ahora serías médico**. A missed chance: **me hubiera gustado ir**, **tendríamos que haber ido**, **te lo perdiste**. And **hubieras** + participle alone is a reproach: **¡hubieras avisado!** — *you should have told me!*' where id = '55b97bb7-34ad-5d9c-8a39-e9ca1dff6cbe' and body_md = '**Si hubieras estudiado, ahora serías…** — and the one you let slip: **me hubiera gustado**, **tendríamos que haber…**, **te lo perdiste**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The most natural way to say what you love about a place: **lo que más me gusta de Buenos Aires es la noche**. The opposite: **lo que menos me gusta es el ruido**. And **lo más** + adjective is *the most … thing*: **lo más lindo del barrio es la plaza**.', title_en = 'Lo que más, lo más' where id = 'a1c0dd99-f02a-5bad-9b95-50478e5f3daa' and body_md = 'The most natural way to say what you love about a place: **lo que más me gusta de Buenos Aires es la noche**. And the opposite: **lo que menos me gusta es el ruido**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A past that went differently, and what it would mean today: **si hubiera ahorrado** (then), **ahora tendría un depto** (now). The first half is **hubiera** + participle; the second is the plain conditional. **A esta altura** — *by now* — goes in the *now* half: **a esta altura estaría jubilado**.', title_en = 'Then and now' where id = 'a0157ee6-1047-52d7-bc9d-1f2a42b1f1d5' and body_md = 'A past that went differently, and what it would mean today: **si hubiera ahorrado** (then), **ahora tendría un depto** (now). The first half is *hubiera* + participle, the second the plain conditional.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'On its own, **es que…** is the start of every porteño excuse: **—¿No venís? —Es que laburo temprano.**' where id = '1d62d696-8f13-5ebd-932a-c477849a8b15' and body_md = 'On its own, **es que…** is the start of every porteño excuse: **¿no venís? — Es que laburo temprano**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Tell it in the past: **lo que pasó fue que se cortó la luz**. Say what you meant: **lo que quiero decir es que…**. You already know **lo que más** — *what… most*: **lo que más me molestó fue eso**. And **en el fondo** — *deep down* — for the real reason under it.' where id = '83a1fba1-c4e8-509e-834e-ea0696869b8d' and body_md = 'Tell it in the past: **lo que pasó fue que se cortó el subte**. Say what you meant: **lo que quiero decir es que…**. **Lo que más** — *what… most*: **lo que más me molestó fue eso**. And **en el fondo** — *deep down* — for the real reason under it.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**El que avisa no traiciona** — *don''t say I didn''t warn you*. You say it while you give the warning. Literally: *the one who warns you doesn''t betray you*. Two more you''ll hear in Buenos Aires: **sobre gustos no hay nada escrito** — *everyone has their own taste*; **el que quiere celeste, que le cueste** — *if you want something good, you have to work for it*.' where id = 'e6b7166a-1ef7-5de5-90cc-d87a7c023771' and body_md = '**El que avisa no traiciona** — *don''t say I didn''t warn you*. You say it while you give the warning. Literally: *the one who warns you doesn''t betray you*. Two you''ll hear every week in Buenos Aires: **sobre gustos no hay nada escrito** — *there''s no accounting for taste*; **el que quiere celeste, que le cueste** — *if you want the good stuff, it will cost you*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Como dice el dicho** — *as the saying goes* — and then the one that fits: **cada loco con su tema** — *to each their own*; **no hay dos sin tres** — *there''s always a third time*; **el que no llora no mama** — *if you don''t ask, you don''t get*.' where id = 'a52eadb9-c139-52a4-b142-3865a13646ae' and body_md = '**Como dice el dicho** — *as the saying goes* — and then the one that fits: **cada loco con su tema** — *to each their own*; **no hay dos sin tres** — *it happened twice, it''ll happen again*; **el que no llora no mama** — *if you don''t ask, you don''t get*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Más vale pájaro en mano que cien volando** — *one sure thing is better than a hundred possible ones*; **a caballo regalado no se le miran los dientes** — *you don''t complain about a gift*; **ojos que no ven, corazón que no siente** — *what you don''t know can''t hurt you*; **del dicho al hecho hay mucho trecho** — *easier said than done*. **El que se quema con leche, ve una vaca y llora** — *after a bad experience, you''re scared of anything similar*. For someone who complicates everything: **buscarle la quinta pata al gato** — *to look for the cat''s fifth leg*. And when someone walks in: **hablando del rey de Roma…** — *we were just talking about you*.' where id = 'c856ee20-16fd-55e2-88a7-bb617e0c577d' and body_md = '**Más vale pájaro en mano que cien volando** — *one sure thing is better than a hundred possible ones*; **a caballo regalado no se le miran los dientes** — *you don''t complain about a gift*; **ojos que no ven, corazón que no siente** — *what you don''t know can''t hurt you*; **del dicho al hecho hay mucho trecho** — *easier said than done*. **El que se quema con leche, ve una vaca y llora** — *after a bad experience, you''re scared of anything similar*. For someone who complicates everything: **buscarle la quinta pata al gato** — *to look for the cat''s fifth leg*. And when someone walks in: **hablando del rey de Roma…** — *we were just talking about you*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me morí de risa**, **¿de qué te reís?**, **me hizo sentir…** — and **cuanto antes lleguemos, mejor**. **A la larga** — *in the long run*: **a la larga, el esfuerzo rinde**.', title_en = 'Me morí de risa' where id = '2195936f-d3dc-5457-874a-d4ff433f78c3' and body_md = '**Me morí de risa**, **¿de qué te reís?**, **me hizo sentir…** — and **cuanto antes lleguemos, mejor**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Al horno** — *in trouble*; **qué bajón** — *what a shame*; **ni en pedo** — *no way*; **rata** — *stingy*; **manija** — *very excited*; **guita** — *money*; **hacer la gamba** — *to help someone out or keep them company*. All among friends.' where id = '2cdd21ad-467f-5fd7-a33c-ff457fb68650' and body_md = '**Al horno** — *in trouble*; **qué bajón** — *what a shame*; **ni en pedo** — *no way*; **rata** — *stingy*; **careta** — *fake*; **manija** — *very excited*. All among friends.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Something does it *to* you: **me dejó pensando** — *it got me thinking*; **me partió el alma** — *it broke my heart*. And you end up frozen: **me quedé helado** — *I froze, I was stunned*. A woman says **me quedé helada**. The good ones: **me hace bien**, **me da ternura**, and **¡qué alivio!**', title_en = 'Me quedé helado' where id = '0904d601-7430-56cd-9bf0-9e5b17a157e0' and body_md = 'The same shape as **me cayó la ficha** — the feeling happens *to* you: **me quedé helado** — *I froze, I was stunned*; **me dejó pensando** — *it got me thinking*; **me partió el alma** — *it broke my heart*. The good ones: **me hace bien**, **me da ternura**, and **¡qué alivio!**';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Lo que pasó fue que**, **lo que quiero decir es que**, **lo tuyo**, **lo que sea**, **en el fondo**. And three sayings: **cada loco con su tema** — *to each their own*; **no hay dos sin tres** — *there''s always a third time*; **hablando del rey de Roma** — *we were just talking about you*.', title_en = 'Lo que pasó fue que…' where id = 'b1b445dc-605c-502f-a4b3-fc7a72caf676' and body_md = '**Lo que pasó fue que**, **lo que quiero decir es que**, **lo tuyo**, **lo que sea** — and **como dice el dicho**, **cada loco con su tema**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Mejor todavía** — *even better*: **¿es gratis? Mejor todavía**; also **mejor así** — *better this way*. *Tanto mejor* says the same but sounds bookish. To **evitar** the **hora pico**, you go early; the place **se llena** fast; and leaving early, the day **rinde** — *goes further*. **Ganar tiempo** is *to save time*: **con el subte ganás tiempo**.' where id = 'b9bc5c55-0b39-5996-a6ed-71dd17a76fb0' and body_md = '**Mejor todavía** — *even better*: **¿es gratis? Mejor todavía**; also **mejor así** — *better this way*. *Tanto mejor* says the same but sounds bookish. To **evitar** the **hora pico**, you go early; the place **se llena** fast; and leaving early, the day **rinde** — *goes further*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me da cosa** has two uses. Doing something feels awkward: **me da cosa pedirle plata** — *I feel awkward asking him for money*. Or a thing gives you a bad feeling: **ese perro me da cosa** — *that dog makes me uneasy*. **Me pone mal** — *it makes me sad*. **Me quedé con las ganas** — *I missed out, and I still want to*.', title_en = 'Me da cosa' where id = '6b55c1f4-870b-5f43-8afa-9decf186dca1' and body_md = '**Me da cosa** — *I feel awkward about it, it makes me uneasy*. Mostly with an infinitive: **me da cosa pedirle plata** — *I feel bad asking him for money*; and about a thing: *ese perro me da cosa*. **Me pone mal** — *it gets me down*. **Me quedé con las ganas** — *I missed out, and I still want to*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Reírse** is *to laugh*: **me río mucho con vos** — *I laugh a lot with you*. You already know **me reí** and **nos reímos**; with *vos* in the past it is **te reíste**: **¿de qué te reíste?** **Llorar** is *to cry*: **lloré con esa película**.', title_en = 'Me río, te reíste' where id = '8845c3ad-88ce-52bb-b23a-7f37ca96a528' and body_md = '**Reírse** is *to laugh*: **me río mucho con vos** — *I laugh a lot with you*; **me reí un montón**, **nos reímos de todo**; **¿te reíste?** **Llorar** is *to cry*: **lloré con la película**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Many porteños have an **abuelo** or **bisabuelo** who **llegó en barco** from Italy or Spain. An Italian, or anyone with an Italian surname, is a **tano** or a **tana**: *mi abuelo era tano*. That''s why a porteño talks with his hands and eats ñoquis on the 29th.' where id = 'a5efa082-ec6d-55de-8585-829fc1b6a047' and body_md = 'Most porteños have an **abuelo** or **bisabuelo** who **llegó en barco** from Italy or Spain. An Italian, or anyone with an Italian surname, is a **tano** or a **tana**: *mi abuelo era tano*. That''s why a porteño talks with his hands and eats ñoquis on the 29th.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The family story runs in the third person plural: **se escaparon de la guerra**, **se instalaron en un conventillo** — *an old shared house where each poor family rented one room* — and **trabajaron en el puerto**. One person: **se instaló**. They left **pobreza** behind, **mantuvieron** the language and the traditions, and **guardaron** the photos of the ship. *Conservaron* says the same, but it is a written word.' where id = '4039fa21-f933-5aec-877d-701a109a210b' and body_md = 'The family story runs in the third person plural: **se escaparon de la guerra**, **se instalaron en un conventillo** — *a crowded tenement house* — and **trabajaron en el puerto**. One person: **se instaló**. They left **pobreza** behind, **mantuvieron** the language and the traditions, and **guardaron** the photos of the ship. *Conservaron* says the same, but it is a written word.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Acampamos al lado de un lago**, **hicimos dedo**; **¿te convido un mate?** — but **no hiervas el agua**. A **carpa** is a camping tent; on the beach in Mar del Plata it is also a rented shade tent.' where id = '9f9ceb73-2afc-50c6-b957-5e19f23e93c9' and body_md = '**Acampamos al lado de un lago**, **hicimos dedo**; **¿te convido un mate?** — but **no hiervas el agua**. On the beach, a **carpa** is a rented beach tent (a cabana).';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Looking back, a finished thing takes the preterite: **al principio me costó** — *it was hard at first* — **pero me adapté** — *I adapted*. How things were takes the imperfect: *al principio era raro*. Now **me siento como en casa**. Say it **de corazón**.' where id = '36794004-344e-51d8-96d4-0a9ba3a15337' and body_md = 'Looking back is the preterite: **al principio me costó** — *it was hard at first* — **pero me adapté** — *I adapted*. Now **me siento como en casa**. Say it **de corazón**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Lograr** — *to manage something hard, to achieve*: **¡lo lograste!** — *you did it!* And your own line: **¡lo logré!** — *I did it!* Then **felicitaciones** — *congratulations* — or, among friends, just **¡grande!**' where id = 'bb475835-3596-5744-abe5-6a802edce685' and body_md = '**Lograr** — *to manage, to pull off*: **¡lo lograste!** — *you did it!* And your own line: **¡lo logré!** — *I did it!* Then **felicitaciones** — *congratulations* — or, among friends, just **¡grande!**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When people notice your **acento** less and less, someone will say **ya sos de acá** — *you''re one of us now*. Take it: it''s the highest praise the city has.' where id = '8e491aaa-a221-5434-b38f-8e4c46b7a2ea' and body_md = 'When your **acento** gives you away less and less, someone will say **ya sos de acá** — *you''re one of us now*. Take it: it''s the highest praise the city has.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Big moments: **se recibió** — *graduated*; **se comprometieron** — *got engaged*; **se jubiló** — *retired*. And the feelings: **se emocionó** — *got emotional*; **me llegó** — *it touched me*.' where id = 'd3c1b17e-2938-5068-9e90-ab4c6a0edcec' and body_md = '**Se recibió**, **se comprometieron**, **se jubiló** — and **se emocionó**, **nos emocionamos**, **me llegó**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me llegó** — *it really touched me*: **tu mensaje me llegó un montón**. Careful: plain **me llegó tu mensaje** just means *I got your message*.' where id = 'a25e7141-158e-5b98-ad99-7895076ecc1f' and body_md = '**Me llegó** — *it really touched me*: **tu mensaje me llegó un montón**. Careful: plain **me llegó tu mensaje** just means *I got your message*. Say it **de todo corazón**. **Sos un orgullo** — *you make us proud*. After the **discurso**, my dad **me abrazó** — *hugged me* — and the **felicidad** was all over the room.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Emocionarse** is mostly *to be moved, to get emotional* (it can also mean *to get excited*): **me emocioné en el casamiento**. **Se me puso la piel de gallina** — *I got goosebumps*. Also **me dio piel de gallina** — *it gave me goosebumps*.' where id = 'cca2ccce-cf17-599f-8925-4e509a09fbef' and body_md = '**Emocionarse** is mostly *to be moved, to get emotional* (it can also mean *to get excited*): **me emocioné en el casamiento**. **Se me puso la piel de gallina** — *I got goosebumps*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estoy orgulloso de vos** — *I''m proud of you*. A woman says **orgullosa** and **agradecida**. **Agradecido** — *grateful*: **estoy muy agradecida**. Grateful *to* a person: **agradecido con vos**. Grateful *for* a thing: **agradecida por el regalo**.' where id = '73a05d53-1c14-5efb-ad11-2e0630cff1d7' and body_md = '**Estoy orgulloso de vos** — *I''m proud of you*. **Agradecido** — *grateful*: **estoy muy agradecida**. Grateful *to* a person: **agradecido con vos**. Grateful *for* a thing: **agradecida por el regalo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| a fact — normal verb | a maybe — subjunctive |
| Aunque **llueve**, entreno. | Aunque **llueva**, entreno igual. |
| Por más que me **cuesta**, sigo. | Por más que me **cueste**, sigo. |
| Aunque no **tengo** ganas, voy. | Aunque no **tenga** ganas, voy igual. |

**Aunque sea** — *even just*: *aunque sea un rato*.', title_en = 'Aunque: fact or maybe' where id = '5d9cf103-d9b8-5f59-afa3-d19b7d920777' and body_md = '| a fact — normal verb | a maybe — subjunctive |
| Aunque **llueve**, entreno. | Aunque **llueva**, entreno igual. |
| Por más que me **cuesta**, sigo. | Por más que me **cueste**, sigo. |
| Aunque no **tengo** ganas, voy. | Aunque no **tenga** ganas, voy igual. |

**Por más que** is a stronger *aunque*. **Aunque sea** — *even just*: *aunque sea un rato*. **Sin embargo, así y todo** start the other half.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Buscar** is *to look for* — *tengo que buscar laburo* — and also *to pick someone up*: *tengo que buscar a mi hijo*, *tienen que buscar a sus hijos*.', title_en = 'Buscar' where id = '3910aabd-7879-56ce-9fd0-298db2aac86c' and body_md = '*Tener que* works with every person: *tenemos que laburar*, *los médicos tienen que ayudar*. **Buscar** also means *to pick someone up*: *tengo que buscar a mi hijo*.';
